{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-artificial-intelligence-and-software-engineering/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Artificial Intelligence and Software Engineering",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08344 Your role The successful candidate will join the SERVAL research group and contribute to research and development activities at the intersection of Agentic AI, AI Security, Trustworthy AI, Software Engineering, and Cybersecurity. The group is developing novel methods, tools, and platforms to support the safe deployment of AI systems in real-world environments. Current research activities focus on topics such as: AI agents and computer-use agents Security, robustness, and trustworthiness of AI systems Evaluation, benchmarking, and testing of AI systems Runtime monitoring and governance of AI agents Formal specification and verification techniques for AI-enabled systems AI systems for enterprise and cybersecurity applications AI compliance, risk assessment, and trustworthy AI engineering Your profile The candidate will contribute to both fundamental research and the development of practical software platforms and demonstrators in collaboration with industrial and public-sector partners. The position holder will be required to perform the following tasks: Act as the main contributor to a software development project related to agentic AI, with the aim to develop it into a real product Design and build demonstrators to showcase academic and industrial research outcomes. Prototype with emerging technologies, frameworks, and methods related to AI and software engineering Contribute to team knowledge-sharing efforts and promote best practices in software development We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Full CV, including list of publications Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Research statement and topics of particular interest to the candidate (300 words) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. The University of Luxembourg is committed to achieving gender parity among its staff. Should candidates present equivalent profiles, preference will be given to female candidates in all departments where gender parity is not yet achieved. The University of Luxembourg embraces inclusion and diversity as key values. We are fully committed to removing any discriminatory barrier related to gender, and not only, in recruitment and career progression of our staff. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 18 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08344 . About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-bioimaging-platform/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Bioimaging Platform",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Luxembourg Centre for Systems Biomedicine (LCSB) Job reference UOL08503 Your role Develop, implement and optimize innovative microscopy, cytometry and image analysis workflows to support cutting-edge biomedical research Design, maintain and continuously improve reproducible image and cytometry data analysis pipelines using state-of-the-art open-source and commercial software Evaluate, validate and implement emerging imaging technologies, image analysis methods and computational workflows, including AI-based approaches Collaborate closely with researchers to design microscopy and cytometry experiments and develop tailored solutions for complex biological questions Provide scientific expertise in microscopy, cytometry, quantitative image analysis and experimental design Contribute to the evaluation, validation and implementation of new instrumentation, software solutions and quality assurance procedures within the Bioimaging Platform Develop, maintain and disseminate standard operating procedures (SOPs), best practice guidelines and quality control protocols Ensure the maintenance, documentation and continuous optimization of computational tools and analysis workflows deployed by the platform Contribute to collaborative research projects, scientific publications and competitive grant applications Deliver advanced training courses, workshops and scientific consultations on microscopy, cytometry and quantitative image analysis Contribute to the continuous innovation and scientific excellence of the Bioimaging Platform Your profile A University Master’s degree (or officially recognized equivalent diploma) in biology, biomedical engineering, biophysics, bioinformatics, computer science, physics, engineering, or a related discipline Proven experience with advanced light microscopy and/or flow cytometry, including quantitative image and/or cytometry data analysis Experience developing and implementing quantitative image analysis workflows using open-source platforms Programming skills in Python, MATLAB, or another scientific programming language Excellent command of English is required Preferred but not mandatory: Experience applying deep learning or AI-based methods for image segmentation, object detection, classification or quantitative bioimage analysis Experience with confocal, live-cell, high-content, super-resolution or light-sheet microscopy Experience with FlowJo and other cytometry data analysis software Experience developing automated and reproducible image analysis workflows Knowledge of image data management and FAIR data principles Experience contributing to collaborative research projects, scientific publications and competitive grant applications Experience working in a research infrastructure, core facility or interdisciplinary research environment We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08503 . About the LCSB The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Centre for Systems Biomedicine (LCSB) is an interdisciplinary research centre of the University of Luxembourg. We conduct fundamental and translational research in the field of Systems Biology and Biomedicine – in the lab, in the clinic and in silico. We focus on neurodegenerative processes and are especially interested in Alzheimer’s and Parkinson’s disease and their contributing factors. The LCSB recruits talented scientists from various disciplines: computer scientists, mathematicians, biologists, chemists, engineers, physicists and clinicians from more than 50 countries currently work at the LCSB. We excel because we are truly interdisciplinary, and together we contribute to science and society. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-ai-driven-cyber-range-engineering/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in AI-Driven Cyber Range Engineering",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08489 Your role Design, develop and maintain the software components implementing scenario generation, aggregation and gap-analysis functionalities in cyber-range environments Analyse existing project documentation, architecture decisions and requirements and translate them into consistent technical specifications and design choices Contribute to and maintain the overall system architecture, using modelling tools/notations to formalize components, interfaces and dependencies between the parts developed by SnT and those developed by partners Define and track the technical requirements and interface contracts expected from partners for their part of the architecture, and follow up to ensure their developments remain aligned and compatible with the overall integration Integrate AI models developed by the research team into functional, deployable prototypes Contribute to technical documentation, demonstrations and dissemination material Provide technical support to project coordination, reporting and deliverable preparation The project aims to enhance the capabilities of cyber-ranges, platforms increasingly used to train students and professionals to keep pace with emerging and complex cyber threats. While robust infrastructures now exist to run cybersecurity exercises, creating and managing training scenarios remains a largely manual, time-consuming process, from scenario design and content generation to execution, monitoring and feedback. The project addresses this by integrating automation into multiple facets of cyber-range operation: federating infrastructures to deploy complex scenarios across multiple platforms, generating and combining scenario content and integrating automated agents that assist or challenge trainees during exercises. The Research and Development Specialist will be primarily responsible for the engineering effort of the project: turning the models and methods defined by the research team into robust, usable software, and ensuring these tools are properly integrated with partners’ platforms and infrastructures. The overall system to be built is a large, multi-partner architecture combining components developed by SnT with components developed by academic and industry partners. The position holder will own the design of a significant part of this architecture, while also having to take into account requirements, constraints and interfaces already defined earlier in the project, and to make sure the parts under the responsibility of the other partners are specified clearly enough and progress in a way that is compatible with the overall integration. The project will involve regular travelling in Europe. Your profile The candidate should hold a MSc degree or equivalent in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Telecommunications, or a related field. What we’re looking for: A collaborative team player with a desire to make a personal impact within our interdisciplinary research group A motivated candidate who can work independently and efficiently, and is proactive in solving engineering problems Self-initiative, creativity, curiosity, flexibility and enthusiasm to work Knowledge and Experience : The ideal candidate should have some knowledge and/or experience in one or several of the following areas: Strong software engineering and development skills Ability to read, interpret and work from long technical documents (specifications, requirements, architecture documents), including those produced by other partners or at earlier stages of a project Experience with architecture/requirements modelling tools and notations to formalize components, interfaces and dependencies Experience integrating heterogeneous systems, APIs or tools within a common platform Ability to track technical dependencies across multiple contributors and proactively flag integration risks Comfortable working on collaborative projects and respecting deadlines for deliverables The following qualifications of the applicant are a bonus: Experience with cyber-range platforms or virtual training/lab infrastructures Experience integrating AI/ML models into production or research software Familiarity with description/interchange formats and ontologies (e.g. YAML/JSON schemas, MITRE ATT&CK-based modelling) Experience working in multi-partner, international collaborative projects Language Skills : Excellent command of English is required. Knowledge of either French, German or Luxembourgish will be appreciated but are not a requirement to apply. For further information, please contact us at Jerome.francois@uni.lu and lama.sleem@uni.lu We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter, including a statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (approx. 300 words) Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken (Bachelor’s and Master’s degree or equivalent) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. The University of Luxembourg is committed to achieving gender parity among its staff. Should candidates present equivalent profiles, preference will be given to female candidates in all departments where gender parity is not yet achieved. The University of Luxembourg embraces inclusion and diversity as key values. We are fully committed to removing any discriminatory barrier related to gender, and not only, in recruitment and career progression of our staff. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08489 . About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The SnT is seeking a Research and Development Specialist to support the engineering work within the SEDAN group ( https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/sedan ). This is a fully funded position with a duration of 2 years, within a collaborative project involving leading academic and industry partners in the field of cybersecurity and cyber-defense across Europe. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/building-technical-specialist/": {
      "title": "Building Technical Specialist",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Permanent contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Central Administration Job reference UOL08127 Your role Coordinate the monitoring of maintenance operations, regulatory inspections, and compliance for assigned real estate sites in technical areas such as HVAC, special gases, building system regulations, and electricity. Ensure quality service delivery in UNI’s buildings, including offices, classrooms, and high-standard facilities such as BSL1/BSL2 laboratories, clean rooms, and animal houses. Integrate energy management, sustainability, and daily safety considerations into your mission. Monitor and report on key operating parameters required by internal customers, ensuring smooth infrastructure operation and building sustainability. Periodically report on installation status, incidents, faults, and solutions, either independently or in coordination with service providers. In collaboration with internal customers and service providers, develop business continuity plans by assessing risks of technical failures and their operational impact. Plan and coordinate infrastructure work and modifications, ensuring future maintenance conditions are met for security and safety equipment. Ensure compliance with technical specifications, performance standards, budgets, and deadlines in all activities. Actively contribute to the continuous improvement of maintenance and upkeeping policy for assets, focusing on reliability, safety, quality, customer satisfaction, and profitability. Manage all administrative tasks and documentation related to technical activities and play an active role in preparing relevant budgets. Your profile Education: Minimum BAC+3 in technical/building maintenance – Experience: At least 5 years in building maintenance Expertise in HVAC, fluids/gas, and regulation systems Expertise in the electrical field – power and low-current installations – is an asset Experience in laboratory infrastructures is an asset Technical Skills: Knowledge of AutoCAD and Microsoft 365, ticketing systems is an advantage Proficient in writing reports/presentations Experience in drafting technical sections of tender documents is an asset Key Qualities: Solution-Oriented & Collaborative: proactive in identifying and resolving issues, proposing improvements Keen on customer satisfaction through clear, professional communication Organized, rigorous, and able to multitask and prioritize effectively Ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, stakeholders, and service providers Job Requirements: Strong on-site presence to gain in-depth knowledge of technical infrastructures Occasional work outside regular hours, including Saturdays On-call duty, to ensure 24/7 operations and interventions Languages: French (C1 – independent) English (B2 – advanced; required for meetings) We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Permanent Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Building technical specialist Job Reference: UOL08127 . About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/chercheur-doctoral-en-etudes-migratoires-et-genre/": {
      "title": "Chercheur Doctoral en études Migratoires Et Genre",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) Job reference UOL08318 Your role Préparer une thèse de doctorat en études migratoires liées au genre en anglais ou en français Participer aux activités d’enseignement Participer à l’organisation de certaines activités du MIS Le doctorant sera membre de la FHSE ( https://www.uni.lu/fhse-en/) et associé au MIS ( https://mis.uni.lu/ ).L’affiliation au département dépendra de l’affiliation du directeur de thèse à l’Université du Luxembourg. Une cotutelle avec l’université du Cap-Vert est possible, l’affiliation dépendra donc de l’affiliation départementale du directeur de thèse dans cette université. Les propositions de sujets de recherche utilisant des méthodes qualitatives et/ou quantitatives sont bienvenues. Pour toute question complémentaire, veuillez contacter le professeur Harlan Koff : harlan.koff@uni.lu Your profile Citoyen et résident du Cap-Vert : une preuve de ces deux éléments sera exigée du candidat sélectionné Master en sciences humaines ou sociales – psychologie, anthropologie, sciences de l’éducation, sciences politiques, sociologie, histoire Exigences linguistiques opérationnelles : Maîtrise de l’anglais et/ou du français Éligibilité académique (mémoire de thèse) : Les candidats doivent démontrer une maîtrise d’au moins le niveau B2 dans la langue de leur thèse. Pour plus de détails et la liste des certificats acceptés, veuillez consulter la page « Candidature à l’admission – doctorants ». We offer Une université moderne et dynamique, dotée d’une atmosphère personnelle et inclusive. Un caractère multilingue et international. Un personnel issu de plus de 90 pays. Membre du réseau The Guild of European Research-Intensive Universities . Un environnement de recherche exceptionnel, soutenu par un personnel qualifié et des équipements de haute qualité. De solides liens avec les secteurs professionnels et le marché du travail luxembourgeois. Un campus urbain unique doté d’infrastructures excellentes. Un partenaire pour la société et l’industrie. Coopération avec les institutions européennes, des entreprises innovantes, le centre financier, ainsi qu’un large éventail de partenaires non académiques, incluant des ministères, des collectivités locales, des associations et des ONG. How to apply Les candidatures doivent inclure : Un curriculum vitae Une lettre de motivation présentant votre intérêt pour ce sujet de thèse doctorale et expliquant en quoi vos qualifications et vos aspirations correspondent à son orientation académique Le relevé de notes et l’ensemble des résultats obtenus dans les cours suivis au niveau universitaire Proposition de projet de thèse d’une page sur la migration et le genre Les candidatures anticipées sont fortement encouragées, car elles seront traitées au fur et à mesure de leur réception. Veuillez postuler officiellement EN LIGNE via le système RH. Les candidatures par e-mail ne seront pas prises en compte. Toutes les personnes qualifiées sont encouragées à postuler. Conformément à nos valeurs, l’Université du Luxembourg promeut une culture inclusive. Nous encourageons les candidatures de personnes de tous horizons et nous nous engageons à garantir l’égalité et le respect de nos employés et étudiants. Informations générales : Type de contrat : contrat à durée déterminée – 36 mois Temps de travail : temps plein, 40 heures par semaine Lieu : Belval Campus Intitulé interne : Doctoral Researcher Référence du poste : UOL08318 Le salaire brut annuel pour chaque doctorant à l’UL est de 41 976 EUR (temps plein). About us L’Université du Luxembourg est une université de recherche internationale au caractère résolument multilingue et interdisciplinaire. La Faculté des sciences humaines, des sciences de l’éducation et des sciences sociales (FHSE) de l’Université du Luxembourg rassemble des expertises issues des sciences humaines, de la linguistique, des sciences cognitives ainsi que des sciences sociales et de l’éducation. Des personnes issues de 20 disciplines différentes travaillent au sein de la Faculté. Parallèlement à l’approche disciplinaire, une culture de recherche interdisciplinaire très ambitieuse a été développée. La recherche et l’enseignement de la faculté se concentrent sur des questions sociales, économiques, politiques et éducatives, avec l’objectif commun de contribuer à une société inclusive, ouverte et inventive. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/phd-candidate-for-radar-based-4d-imaging-with-advanced-massive-mimo-signal-processing/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher for Radar-Based 4D Imaging with Advanced Massive-MIMO Signal Processing",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07523 Your role The technology of Massive MIMO, through the deployment of numerous antennas at both the transmit (Tx) and receive (Rx) chains, has revolutionized wireless communications by significantly improving capacity and reliability, making it a favored option for various applications, including 5G. This technology has opened exciting new possibilities for 4D (three-dimensional space + Doppler) imaging using mmWave radar sensors, with exceptional spatial and temporal resolution. By utilizing a large number of antennas to transmit and receive signals, Massive MIMO radar can focus energy toward the intended target, minimizing interference from other sources. This enables the sensor to capture fine details about an object’s position, velocity, and movement direction, which can be invaluable for applications such as medical imaging, autonomous driving, in-car monitoring, industrial automation, and security surveillance. The research, called “R4DAR,” aims to leverage emerging 4D imaging technology with Massive MIMO to create image-like radar observations in a more feasible way. The project focuses on addressing existing gaps in knowledge of Massive MIMO for radar, functional limitations, and sensing robustness while incorporating new features and achieving lower system costs. More information on the project: https://radarmimo.com/4d-imaging-automotive-mimo-radar/ The selected PhD candidate will work on one of the following research topic: Optimal antenna placement and waveform design for Massive MIMO 4D imaging radar sensors This PhD research will focus on optimizing antenna placement and waveform design for Massive MIMO 4D imaging radars. It will involve investigating different optimization tools, antenna configurations, and waveform parameters to maximize the radar system’s performance regarding accuracy, resolution, and range. Structure and methodology: The PhD student will receive guidance from the advisory committee on prior-art and challenges in Massive MIMO 4D imaging radar They will address these challenges by optimizing waveforms and antenna placements Expected Outcomes: The PhD student will be the first author on at least two journal publications and four conference publications The student will support validation activities by demonstrating the effectiveness of their research in real-world applications The ideal candidate should have a strong background in radar technology, antenna design, and signal processing. Excellent programming skills, particularly in MATLAB or Python, would be beneficial. Your profile The candidate should possess (or be in the process of completing) an MSc degree or equivalent in Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, or Physics with an electromagnetic background Strong theoretical knowledge in some of the following areas: Radar Systems and Signal Processing Optimization methodologies Machine Learning and Deep Learning Development skills in MATLAB/Python/C++ are required Exposure to the latest signal processing techniques, linear algebra, and deep learning is desirable Experience with hardware prototyping using mmWave radar sensors and USRPs is a plus Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae – including a list of publications, bachelor/master thesis, and names (with contact information including email addresses) of references Cover letter Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Research statement and topics of particular interest to the candidate (300 words) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL07523 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 43445 (full time). About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The SPARC group in SnT is pursuing research on signal processing applications in radar and communication systems in partnership with national and international academic and industrial collaborators. Updated information about the recent activities of SPARC can be found here: www.radarmimo.com/ . The group has been working on mmWave radar sensors in different applications, including automotive, indoor sensing, in-cabin monitoring, occupancy sensing, drones, multi-copters, gesture recognition, smart buildings, smart street lighting, smart factories, healthcare, and robotics. The emerging radar sensors in use by the group employ multiple-input multiple-output (MIMO) technology and can be connected to build a distributed and cooperative network. To develop signal processing techniques, the group researchers use real data captured by available radar modules at the lab or custom-built MIMO radar with the flexibility to change the transmit waveform and signal processing units on the fly. Personnel at SPARC have contributed to several seminal papers, book chapters, and books in the fields of waveform optimization, vital signs monitoring, joint radar and communications, sparse arrays, interference modeling, 4D imaging radars, distributed sensing, and tracking. SPARC has also collaborated with long-term industry partners such as IEE S.A ( www.iee.lu ), University of Naples Federico II, US Air Force Laboratories, TU Berlin, and TU Munich, among others. SPARC personnel have also been involved in European Research Council (ERC) Advanced Grant and ERC Proof-of-Concept activities. Recently, an alumnus of the group received the Excellent Thesis Award from the University of Luxembourg. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-engineering-sciences-specializing-in-energy-transition-in-the-building-heating-sector/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Engineering Sciences Specializing in Energy Transition in the Building Heating Sector",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08415 Your role Your research will involve the collection and analysis of real-world data, as well as the application of digital, physical, and data-driven modelling approaches to develop and evaluate solutions for decarbonising the heating sector, with a particular focus on the existing building stock. Your Mission: Conduct high-quality research on the energy transition and decarbonisation of the building heating sector Develop and apply modelling and simulation methods to analyse future energy system scenarios Collect, process, and interpret real-world data to support your research analysis Collaborate with industrial and academic partners at national and international level Disseminate research outcomes through publications in scientific journals and presentations at international conferences Contribute to teaching activities, including approximately 1–2 contact hours per week or the equivalent through student supervision Your profile A Master’s degree in Engineering: Energy, Mechanical, Electrical or a related field Solid background in the energy domain, especially building energy Interest and skills in numerical modelling Operational Language Requirements: Excellent command of English (C1); a good knowledge of either German or French (B1) is a strong asset Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08415 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine.Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. The Department of Engineering (DoE) is a dynamic, interdisciplinary group engaged in civil, electrical and mechanical engineering, driving forward innovative research and solutions. It also has an internationally leading profile in computational science and engineering. We develop cutting-edge technologies, promoting the sustainable and economical use of resources, and meeting the technological demands of Luxembourg, the Greater Region, and beyond. Nearly all research projects are supported by a network of national and international partnerships, several with public or industrial stakeholders. At the University, the Department cooperates across faculties and with the interdisciplinary centres. In particular, the new interdisciplinary centre focused on complex environmental systems opens up significant opportunities for future collaborations. The Research Group for Building Energy and Building Services Engineering, led by Prof. Dr Frank Scholzen within the Department of Engineering of the Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine, is seeking a highly motivated Doctoral Researcher (PhD candidate). As a doctoral researcher, you will be enrolled in the Doctoral School in Science and Engineering within the doctoral programme in Engineering Sciences, which provides interdisciplinary, internationally competitive research training in a collaborative academic environment. The PhD project focuses on the energy transition in the building heating sector, a key pillar of the decarbonisation of the European energy system. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-food-literacy-behaviour-change-and-sustainable-lifestyle/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Food Literacy, Behaviour Change and Sustainable Lifestyle",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) Job reference UOL08510 Your role Conduct an original PhD research project leading to a doctoral degree Carry out literature reviews on food literacy, sustainable consumption and behavioural change Design and implement qualitative and mixed-methods research Conduct interviews, focus groups, participant observation and surveys Analyse qualitative and quantitative datasets Contribute to stakeholder workshops and co-creation activities Publish scientific articles in peer-reviewed journals Participate in doctoral training activities and the University’s doctoral programme Contribute to project reports, policy briefs and dissemination activities Your profile Master’s degree in Sociology, Cultural Anthropology, Political Sciences, History and/or Geography in the field of food studies or related study areas Experience in research project management and conduct, ideally in interdisciplinary contexts In-depth knowledge of Luxembourg’s foodscape, both of the existing interrelations and the cultural and socio-economic stakes, is a prerequisite Previous research work on sustainable food practices and system is a plus Experience and excellent skills in qualitative methods, e.g., individual and group interviews, oral history, ethnography, participant observation, focus groups, as well as good knowledge of quantitative methods – descriptive statistics Interest in food studies, transformative research, agroecological and food system transition studies, practice theory, political ecology, theory of change, as well as governance, governmentality and policy coherence approaches Operational Language Requirements: Excellent command of English is required Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08510 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About the FHSE The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) at the University of Luxembourg brings together expertise from the humanities, linguistics, cognitive sciences, social and educational sciences. People from across 20 disciplines are working within the Faculty. Along with the disciplinary approach a very ambitious interdisciplinary research culture has been developed. The faculty’s research and teaching focuses on social, economic, political and educational issues with the common goal of contributing to an inclusive, open and resourceful society. The research project PALATE (Participatory Actions for Lifestyle Adaptation & Transition Engagement) explores how participatory governance structures, food democracy initiatives and multi-stakeholder collaboration contribute to sustainable food-system transformation in Luxembourg. The project seeks to generate actionable knowledge for policymakers, practitioners and civil society while advancing scientific understanding of food sovereignty, food governance and sustainability transitions. It contributes to Social Readiness withing the overall Climate Nexus Framework, by examining food-related behavioural change and participatory transitions toward sustainable lifestyles. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-geographic-information-systems-and-fintech/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Geographic Information Systems and Fintech",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08402 Your role The successful person will be enrolled in the PhD program in Computer Science and Computer Engineering with a specialisation in Information Systems (IS) and they will contribute to an industry partnership with Banque Centrale du Luxembourg (BCL), focusing on cash infrastructures and financial services. In this context, the candidate will primarily, but not exclusively, use research methods grounded in geospatial economics and econometrics, as well as IS research. The person may also conduct surveys and/or interviews with relevant stakeholders. In addition, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in the creation of networking opportunities, such as conferences and other events, and will disseminate results through scientific publications in well-ranked journals and conferences. The individual will also conduct research in the context of Prof. Gilbert Fridgen’s PayPal-FNR PEARL Research Grant and in collaboration with the FutureFinTech National Centre of Excellence in Research and Innovation. In particular, the successful candidate will be integrated into a larger research team on “Financial Technologies (FinTech)” and might collaborate with team members working on related projects. The successful candidate will thus be able to align the skills acquired during the doctorate with their personal goals and interests. For further information, please contact Dr. Martin Brennecke ( martin.brennecke@uni.lu ) and Prof. Dr. Gilbert Fridgen ( gilbert.fridgen@uni.lu ). Your profile Master’s degree in IS or computer science, preferably with prior coursework in IS, and web design or GeoIS, with a strong interest in design-oriented research Foundational knowledge in at least one of the following programming languages/tools: R, Python, QGIS, ArcGIS. Experience (or interest) in web development Interest in applying qualitative and/or quantitative research methods to address research and industry challenges Willingness to work on the partner’s premises in Luxembourg City for 1-2 days per week A collaborative team player with an interest in socio-technical research and a desire to make a personal impact within our research group The commitment to participate in the design and implementation of high-quality solutions that solve significant problems Self-initiative, creativity, curiosity, flexibility and enthusiasm to work Operational Language Requirements: high English-language proficiency (C1/C2, no certificate required) in both written and verbal communication Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter including: A research statement and a list of topics of particular interest to the candidate, followed a concrete research agenda consisting of the planned research activities which are aligned with the topics covered by FINATRAX and ideally aim at the Information Systems discipline should be provided (300 words) A statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (why a doctoral program, why in Luxembourg, minimum 300 words) A statement on the candidate’s motivation for applying for this topic (minimum 300 words) Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month, extendable up to 48 months if required Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08402 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. SnT is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Luxembourg by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. The Centre is rapidly expanding its research activities and is seeking highly motivated doctoral candidates who wish to pursue research in close cooperation with our partners. For further information, you may check: www.securityandtrust.lu. The successful candidate will join the young, vibrant, and interdisciplinary FINATRAX Research Group, which builds bridges between business research and information systems engineering. The group conducts research on the application and the impact of technology on organisations in the private or public sector. Our team consists of international researchers with backgrounds in technology, law, management, economics, and other fields, united by a shared commitment to advancing sustainable technologies that benefit society. For more information, please visit our website: https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/finatrax/research/ Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/marie-curie-postdoctoral-fellow-in-advanced-wireless-communications/": {
      "title": "Marie Curie Postdoctoral Fellow in Advanced Wireless Communications",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08032 Your role Your research interests shall align with one or more of the following areas: Beyond 5G Wireless Communication Systems Non-Terrestrial Communication Systems Intelligent Open Radio Access Networks Dynamic Spectrum Sharing Access-Edge-Cloud Telecom Network Slicing Reconfigurable Intelligent Surfaces Joint Communication and Sensing Software Defined Networks and Network Virtualisation Network Infrastructure Sharing / Routing Strategies Network Performance Monitoring and Demand-based design ML/AI-Based Network Performance Prediction and Resource Provisioning Quantum Communications Optical Communications Key Responsibilities: Analyzing and investigating novel scenarios and use cases, developing novel solutions able to provide a good performance-complexity trade-off for the identified scenarios and use cases. Implementing and developing a software and/or hardware testing environment to compare and evaluate the proposed techniques. Disseminating results through scientific publications and conferences The candidates are expected to actively contribute to the selected research area. Preparing new research proposals to attract follow-up industrial, national and European projects Providing assistance in the supervision of PhD students. Your profile Qualification: The candidate should possess an Ph.D. degree or equivalent in Telecommunications and Computer Science Experience: The successful candidate should have proven experience (in terms of high-ranking journals or international conference proceedings and involvement in research activities) in one or multiple areas mentioned above. In addition, we request the following expertise: Convex/non-convex optimization Signal processing and general communications background Programming skills in MATLAB and/or Python Good writing and oral presentation skills, in English Eligibility requirements of MSCA: Research experience: Maximum of 8 years from the award of first PhD. N.B.: Deductions apply e.g., maternity leave, not working in research Resubmission: Allowed if a proposal scores at least 70% Mobility rule: Must not have resided or carried out main activity in Luxembourg for more than 12 months in the 36 months immediately before their recruitment date, N.B.: includes remote work Only one proposal per individual can be submitted Secondments can take up to one-third of the duration of the fellowship We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08032 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 85176 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. SIGCOM group at SnT, University of Luxembourg, is currently seeking expressions of interest from outstanding PhD students (nearing completion) or early-career postdoctoral researchers who would like to apply for the MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowship 2026 with Prof. Symeon Chatzinotas and/or Prof. Eva Lagunas as Academic Supervisors. The Marie Skłodowska-Curie Postdoctoral Fellowships are a fantastic platform to boost your career: International, inter-sectoral, and interdisciplinary experience Strong training in research and transferable skills Enhanced employability inside and outside academia Opportunities to work on innovative projects and network globally More information is available at: https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/calls/msca-postdoctoral-fellowships-2026 Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/associate-professor-or-assistant-professor-in-clinical-microbiology/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor Or Assistant Professor in Clinical Microbiology",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Professorial Permanent – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08386 Your role The position focuses on innovative, interdisciplinary teaching in clinical microbiology at the bachelor’s level and within medical specialization programmes. The recruited professor will play a central role in establishing teaching and research expertise in areas such as infectious diseases, antimicrobial resistance, and diagnostic microbiology. The successful candidate will lead the development and coordination of clinical microbiology teaching activities across the University’s programmes in medicine and health-related sciences. The role includes the implementation of a state-of-the-art clinical microbiology curriculum, incorporating advanced educational tools such as digital microbiology platforms, virtual labs, simulation-based training, and case-based learning. Working closely with faculty members and clinical partners, the successful candidate will ensure an integrated and cohesive learning experience for students. Research Portfolio The candidate is expected to have an internationally recognised research profile and to develop ambitious research activities in areas including infectious diseases, antimicrobial resistance, hygiene, microbiome science, data-driven health sciences, and digital medicine. Clinical Integration The ideal candidate will have a medical background with relevant clinical experience in microbiology, and a strong commitment to integrating clinical perspectives into education. This includes fostering strong links between teaching, research and clinical practice, thereby enhancing the practical application of clinical microbiology in medical education. The candidate is encouraged to maintain a clinical affiliation while working at the University ensuring strong ties between academia and clinical practice. For further information about the role, please contact: Serge Haan, Head of DHML, Email: serge.haan@uni.lu Your profile An MD with a specialization in microbiology, e.g.: bacteriology, virology, parasitology, and other infectious diseases, and/or a PhD in microbiology, e.g.: bacteriology, virology, parasitology, and other infectious diseases, or a closely related field. Practical experience in diagnostic microbiology and infectious disease management is considered a strong advantage Teaching experience in microbiology and clinical microbiology at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels, ideally within medical or biomedical programs Proven commitment to interdisciplinary and innovative teaching, particularly in integrating clinical microbiology with medicine, life sciences, and public health Demonstrated ability to design and implement new educational courses, including clinical training module and laboratory-based instruction Familiarity with modern teaching methods and tools, such as online learning platforms, simulation-based training, and case-based learning approaches Research focus on infectious diseases, antimicrobial resistance, hygiene, microbiome science, data-driven health sciences, and digital medicine Language requirements The University of Luxembourg is set in a multilingual and multicultural context. The person hired on this position must be proficient in English, and either French or German. The University encourages its staff to learn the other language and provides access to language courses to this end. We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Cover letter, to be addressed to Serge Haan, Head of DHML CV, including any periods of absence from work such as family-related leave and career breaks Short description of profile, key achievements and impact, summarizing main publications, projects, teaching expertise and accomplishments in knowledge transfer relevant to this role (1-3 pages) Statement of planned research, teaching and other activities at the University of Luxembourg (1–3 pages) Lists of publications, research projects, PhD theses supervised and subjects taught Names, contact information and current position of 3 referees who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate their relationship to you We encourage early application. Applications are only accepted online through the HR system. The position will be unposted on 29th October 2026, after which no further applications can be submitted. Applications will be handled in strict confidence. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. Diversity and gender equality The University of Luxembourg embraces inclusion, diversity and gender equality as essential for academic excellence. We are fully committed to removing discriminatory barriers in recruitment and career progression and to advance gender balance among academic staff. Should candidates present equivalent CVs, preference will be given to female candidates in all departments where gender parity is not yet achieved. General information: Contract Type: Professorial – Permanent . This position is offered at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level, depending on profile. Both positions are tenured Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week. Working time will be adapted in accordance with the candidate’s clinical commitments, if applicable Location: Belval Campus Job Reference: UOL08386. The reference should be mentioned in all correspondence Starting date: July 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter About the FSTM The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine. Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. Within the FSTM, the Department of Health, Medicine and Life Sciences (DHML) coordinates all teaching programmes in life sciences, medicine, nursing, radiology and midwifery. The department’s research combines basic and translational, molecular and computational approaches, with a particular focus on cancer biology, while also encompassing clinical research in human health and disease. The DHML cooperates with the national health care centers and leading international biomedical research institutions. As medicine and health are strategic priorities for the University of Luxembourg, the department is actively expanding its education and research activities in these fields, providing exceptional opportunities for medical and biomedical initiatives. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-smart-energy-system-modelling/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Smart Energy System Modelling",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07892 Your role The candidate will work on the the Data-Driven Energy Transition NCER Project (D2ET). This project aims to accelerate the energy transition in Luxembourg by co-creating an ambitious research program. It will utilize a data-driven approach to support decision-making for an optimal energy system, with specific focus on cost-effectiveness, emission reduction, and social acceptability. D2ET will develop a comprehensive digital platform for planning energy transition scenarios, leveraging a consolidated data model and advanced analytics to facilitate strategic decisions with relevant stakeholders. In the context of this project the candidate will design and implement a cutting edge international Energy System Model that delivers comprehensive energy economic insights, supporting further research and development at Finatrax. Supported in a strong team environment the candidate will develop an innovative approach to renewable energy system modelling (based on stochastic optimization), develop scenarios of the energy transition, conduct policy analyses and technology evaluation. The insights will be published in leading international outlets and contribute to shape the energy transition in Luxembourg. For further information, please contact joachim.geske@uni.lu Your profile Master’s degree in Energy Policy, Energy Economics, Information Systems, Mathematics, Operations Research or a related field Strong knowledge of quantitative and/or computational research methods, ideally in numerical optimization and simulation models. Proficiency in one of the major programming languages such as Python A collaborative team player with a desire to make a personal impact within our interdisciplinary research group and our broader economy and society The commitment to participate in the design, implementation, and theoretical elaboration of high-quality solutions that solve significant real-world economic problems in the energy domain Self-initiative, creativity, curiosity, flexibility, and enthusiasm to work Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: A cover letter including: A research statement and a list of topics of particular interest to the candidate, followed a concrete research agenda consisting of the planned research activities which are aligned with the topics covered by FINATRAX and ideally aim at the Information Systems discipline should be provided (300 words) A statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (why a doctoral program, why in Luxembourg, minimum 300 words) A statement on the candidate’s motivation for shaping future electricity markets in Luxembourg and Europe (minimum 300 words) Full CV, including the contact address and work experience Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken (Bachelor’s and Master’s degree or equivalent) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Months (extendable up to 48 months if required) Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL07892 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. FINATRAX is a young, vibrant, and interdisciplinary Research Group, which builds bridges between electricity markets and digital technologies in Luxembourg, together with several industrial and political stakeholders that shape our energy transition. Located at the heart of Europe, the group consists of doctoral and post-doctoral researchers from diverse backgrounds (e.g., economics, business, technology), united in pursuit of sustainable solutions that positively impact and shape a low-carbon economy and society. For more information, please visit our website: https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/finatrax/research/ Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-trustworthy-world-models-for-critical-systems/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Trustworthy World Models for Critical Systems",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08387 Your role The position holder will be required to perform the following tasks/will do research on the following topics: Explore Foundation Machine Learning topics, including designing new architectures, and training algorithms Implement World Models for simulation on multimodal data (vision + tabular, vision + graph) Evaluate the trustworthiness to assess these systems in real-world critical settings. The candidate will contribute to both fundamental research and the development of practical software platforms and demonstrators in collaboration with industrial and public-sector partners. More generally, the PhD thesis is part of a large initiative at Serval and SnT, which aims to support the reliable deployment of AI systems. The subject of the thesis will be “Exploring Trustworthy World Models for multimodal vision-graph-tabular settings”. It will involve exploring methods and approaches for building data-driven and physics-informed World Models for tasks mixing images, text and structured data (graph, tabular), such as simulation of flooding, cancer and power grids. For further information, please contact Dr. Salah Ghamizi: salah.ghamizi@uni.lu Your profile Master in Computer Science. Major in machine learning or computer vision is an asset Strong programming skills Strong analytical skills Industry experience in information and communication technology for energy or healthcare will be considered as an advantage Commitment, team working, a critical mind, and motivation are skills that are more than welcome Knowledge of both the basics and the latest developments of machine learning, in particular foundation models and other generative AI models Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. The University of Luxembourg is committed to achieving gender parity among its staff. Should candidates present equivalent profiles, preference will be given to female candidates in all departments where gender parity is not yet achieved. The University of Luxembourg embraces inclusion and diversity as key values. We are fully committed to removing any discriminatory barrier related to gender, and not only, in recruitment and career progression of our staff. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08387 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The successful candidate will join the SERVAL research group and contribute to research and development activities at the intersection of Generative AI, Multimodal Machine Learning, Trustworthy AI, and physics informed learning. The group is developing novel methods, tools, and platforms to support the safe deployment of AI systems in real-world environments. Current research activities focus on topics such as: Constrained Generative models for graph and tabular data. Security, robustness, and trustworthiness of AI systems Evaluation, benchmarking, and testing of AI systems AI systems for healthcare, energy and financial applications Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-geospatial-economics-and-information-systems/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Geospatial Economics and Information Systems",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08403 Your role The successful candidate will be enrolled in the PhD program in Computer Science and Computer Engineering with a specialisation in Information Systems (IS) and they will contribute to an industry partnership with Banque Centrale du Luxembourg (BCL), focusing on cash infrastructures and financial services. In this context, the candidate will primarily, but not exclusively, use research methods grounded in geospatial economics and econometrics, as well as IS research. The person may also conduct surveys and/or interviews with relevant stakeholders. In addition, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in the creation of networking opportunities, such as conferences and other events, and will disseminate results through scientific publications in well-ranked journals and conferences. The individual will also conduct research in the context of Prof. Gilbert Fridgen’s PayPal-FNR PEARL Research Grant and in collaboration with the FutureFinTech National Centre of Excellence in Research and Innovation. In particular, the successful candidate will be integrated into a larger research team on “Financial Technologies (FinTech)” and might collaborate with team members working on related projects. The successful candidate will thus be able to align the skills that they learn pursuing a doctorate with their personal goals and interests. For further information, please contact Dr. Martin Brennecke ( martin.brennecke@uni.lu ) and Prof. Dr. Gilbert Fridgen ( gilbert.fridgen@uni.lu ). Your profile Master’s degree in economics, geoinformatics, (geographic) IS, economics of IS or related, with an interest in econometrics, geo-spatial analysis, and/or modelling Foundational knowledge in at least one of the following programming languages/tools: STATA, R, Python, QGIS, ArcGIS Interest in applying quantitative (and/or qualitative) research methods to address research and industry challenges Willingness to work on the partner’s premises in Luxembourg City for 1-2 days per week A collaborative team player with an interest in socio-technical research and a desire to make a personal impact within our research group The commitment to participate in the design and implementation of high-quality solutions that solve significant problems Self-initiative, creativity, curiosity, flexibility, and enthusiasm to work Operational Language Requirements: This position requires a high English-language proficiency (C1/C2, no certificate required) in both written and verbal communication Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter including: A statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (why a doctoral program, why in Luxembourg, minimum 300 words) A statement on the candidate’s motivation for applying for this topic (minimum 300 words) Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08403 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. SnT is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Luxembourg by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. The Centre is rapidly expanding its research activities and is seeking highly motivated doctoral candidates who wish to pursue research in close cooperation with our partners. For further information, you may check: www.securityandtrust.lu. Successful candidates will join the young, vibrant, and interdisciplinary FINATRAX Research Group, which builds bridges between business research and information systems engineering. The group conducts research on the application and the impact of technology on organisations in the private or public sector. Our team consists of international researchers with backgrounds in technology, law, management, economics, and other fields, united by a shared commitment to advancing sustainable technologies that benefit society. For more information, please visit our website: https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/finatrax/join-us/ Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-molecular-and-cellular-cancer-immunology/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Molecular and Cellular Cancer Immunology",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08153 Your role Conduct wet-lab research using mouse models and/or cancer patient samples Develop and apply patient-derived 3D models, immune co-cultures, and study cellular interactions via extracellular vesicles Analyze high-throughput datasets using R or similar software tools Present research findings in meetings Document performed experiments in a lab book to ensure reproducibility Contribute to the preparation of scientific reports, grant applications and publications Participate in lab and institutional activities, including seminars, PhD days, and mentoring opportunities Engage actively in the doctoral training program Your profile Master’s degree in a relevant field e.g., immunology, molecular/cell biology, biomedicine, or related disciplines Strong foundation in adaptive immunity, with familiarity with B cell development, antibody structure, immune responses in cancer Hands-on experience with core wet lab techniques: cell culture, PCR, western blotting, and basic functional assays using immune or cancer cell models Working knowledge of flow cytometry for immune cell phenotyping; experience with multi-parameter panels or cell sorting is a plus Understanding of extracellular vesicle biology, ideally in the context of tumor-immune interactions Basic knowledge of how DNA editing/mutagenesis tools e.g. CRISPR, deaminases, repair pathways can contribute to our understanding of biological mechanisms Comfortable working with biological datasets; experience with R, Python, or omics analysis pipelines is advantageous but a keen willingness to learn is equally valued Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08153 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine.Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and environment we live in. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
