    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-economic-and-financial-history-with-focus-on-the-british-virgin-islands/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Economic and Financial History with Focus on the British Virgin Islands",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Luxembourg Center for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) Job reference UOL08487 Your role The doctoral researcher will work under the supervision of Professor Benoît Majerus within the ERC-funded project “Digital archaeology of shell companies: infrastructures of global connections and local networks (DIGSHELL)”. The project seeks to develop a comprehensive history of global tax networks by examining the emergence of multi-jurisdictional spaces in which nation-states, multinational corporations, local financial intermediaries, and international organizations interact to build, maintain, and govern global financial infrastructures. Building on a previous research initiative focused exclusively on Luxembourg, DIGSHELL adopts a broader international perspective through three additional case studies: Panama, Singapore and the British Virgin Islands (BVI). To facilitate the analysis of this extensive corpus, the project will explore advanced data analysis methods, visualization tools, and generative AI technologies, including Large Language Models (LLMs). The doctoral researcher will initially conduct preliminary research and review existing source materials in Luxembourg. This work will subsequently be complemented by extended research stays abroad, involving archival research, fieldwork, and interviews in the respective target country (Panama, Singapore, and the BVI/United Kingdom). Furthermore, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in the creation of networking opportunities, such as conferences and other events, and will disseminate results through scientific publications in well-ranked journals and conferences. For more information on DIGSHELL: https://www.uni.lu/c2dh-en/research-projects/digshell/ For further information on the position, please contact Prof. Benoît Majerus ( benoit.majerus@uni.lu ). Your profile Qualification : The candidate should have completed a master’s degree or equivalent in history, economics, political science, social science or a related field Experience : The ideal candidate should have proven interest in the following topics: digital history, financial history, offshore studies, fiscal studies, network research Operational Language Requirements : Excellent command of English; good working knowledge of French is an asset Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Name, contact information and current position of 1 referee who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate the person’s relationship to you A two-page project proposal (research question, sources, methodology) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08487 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) at the University of Luxembourg is an interdisciplinary research centre committed to high-quality research and public dissemination in the field of contemporary history with a particular focus on digital methods and tools.The C²DH’s ambition is to venture off the beaten track and find new ways of doing, teaching and presenting contemporary history of Luxembourg and the history of Europe in the 20th and 21st centuries. It serves as a catalyst for innovative and creative scholarship and new forms of public dissemination. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-energy-and-green-house-gas-modelling/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Energy and Green House Gas Modelling",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08216 Your role We are seeking a highly motivated Doctoral researcher to develop a generalized green house gas (GHG) model across all sectors to be integrated with the versatile sector coupled energy model, UCB-SEnMod. This spatial and time resolved combined model will enable a holistic view of direct and indirect GHG emissions, whilst considering possible renewable energy integrations. Key responsibilities: Establish requirements, architect, design and code a GHG module to be integrated with the UCB-SEnMod Extract from literature all necessary workflows to be modelled and data that is needed Use the combined model to design scenarios which would reduce GHG emissions Maintain clear documentation and version control for models and results Prepare the module to be used open source Data analysis, figure preparation, manuscript and report drafting and presentation of results at international conferences Engage in collaboration with internal partners – Luxembourg Centre for Socio-Environmental Systems and external partners such the Trier University of Applied Sciences For more information contact: Prof. Phillip Dale ( phillip.dale@uni.lu ) Your profile We are looking for a motivated, independent, scientist or engineer to join our teams working to reduce GHG emissions. You will be supervised by Prof. Phillip Dale (University of Luxembourg) and Prof. te Heesen (Trier University of Applied Sciences) as part of a cotutelle. Masters degree in physics, chemistry, engineering, environmental sciences or related field Familiarity with Python or similar and use of AI tools Strong fundamentals in physical processes Excellent problem-solving and ability to show initiative Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Portfolio or list of relevant projects One-page proposal outlining your approach to the project Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08216 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 43445 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine.Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and environment we live in. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/librarian-2/": {
      "title": "Librarian",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Permanent contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Luxembourg Centre for European Law (LCEL) Job reference UOL08389 Your role As a Librarian, you will be part of the team providing direct support to users in the University libraries. Your main focus will be on user services and information support, complemented by training and guidance in using documentary or information resources. Welcome and advise users at the library front desk (and via e-mail or phone), providing a professional, service-oriented first contact Answer and follow up on users’ information requests and support them in locating and using resources related to the University’s different research, teaching and learning activities Guide users in searching the catalogue, discovery tools and key subject databases; help them refine search strategies and understand available document types Support users with the international interlibrary loan service Provide one-to-one “desk coaching” and short introductory explanations on how to approach literature searches Participate in the organisation and delivery of brief library tours and introductory sessions for students, researchers and other groups Draft and update clear user-oriented documentation on finding and using documentary resources Perform day-to-day circulation operations and ensure correct application of library policies Contribute to the practical management of print collections: receiving and processing new acquisitions, shelving, shelf reading and basic weeding/inventories Assist in maintaining and improving the quality of records and holdings information in the library system, and report issues or inconsistencies Collect and share user feedback, signal problems with services or systems, and propose pragmatic improvements to front-office workflows Support the preparation of usage statistics and reports related to loans, visits and training activities Keep informed about developments in librarianship and in the University’s teaching and research areas and integrate this into daily service Your profile Bachelor’s degree in Library and Information Science, Documentation or a related field, or equivalent professional experience At least 2 years of relevant experience, preferably in an academic or specialised library Good knowledge of front‑office library services and ability to coordinate daily service processes Familiarity with library management systems and discovery tools; comfortable working with online databases and digital resources; knowledge Alma is a strong asset Demonstrated experience in providing user-oriented services and communicating complex information clearly to users with varying levels of knowledge and experience Proven ability to manage user data, bibliographic or item records and administrative processes accurately, reliably and in accordance with established procedures Language Requirements: Excellent command of English (C1) and very good command in at least one of French or German (B2); knowledge of Luxembourgish or any other language at any level would be considered an asset. We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Permanent Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Librarian Job Reference: UOL08389 . About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The LCEL focuses on the interdisciplinary field of European law and uses to full capacity its proximity to key EU institutions in Luxembourg. The new Interdisciplinary Centre (IC) will combine academic excellence and strategic research with impact. The IC will reflect in its strategic focus the European political agenda of a dual (digital and green) transition and topics related to European sovereignty. Complementing the library landscape, the Luxembourg Centre for European Law library, located in the Weicker building (Kirchberg), supports research and teaching activities by providing specialised resources in European Union law, public and private law, and related areas, and by acting as a central hub for scholars, students and practitioners interested in European and international legal studies. The librarian recruited for this position will be based primarily in Weicker, working in close collaboration with colleagues in the LLC and other University areas You will join a committed, international team of more than 35 library and information professionals who are engaged to delivering high-quality services, collections, research support and innovating to meet user needs. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/librarian-specialist-finance-economics-and-law/": {
      "title": "Librarian Specialist Finance, Economics and Law",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Rectorate Job reference UOL08373 Your role The role will focus on ensuring continuity of services, maintaining collection quality and supporting ongoing academic needs. Act as a key contact / interface between the libraries and University stakeholders, including faculty, researchers, students and administrative departments, in particular within the Faculty of Law, Economics & Finance (FDEF) Take ownership of collection plans and budgets for the relevant subject areas, ensuring expertise and added value to faculty Contribute actively to the preparation, update and implementation of collection development strategies, acquisition plans and related documentation, and contribute to defining and adapting practices, tools and approaches based on needs Provide expert advice, research support and information literacy training tailored to the needs of students, researchers and teaching staff, and act as a sparring partner for academic users Reply to enquiries and support users in identifying, accessing and using relevant documentary resources, databases and information tools, providing added‑value guidance and expert advice where needed Create and maintain subject guides, web pages, bibliographies, thematic selections, tutorials and other user‑support material, aligned with the specific needs and priorities of FDEF and related disciplines Monitor trends in teaching, learning and research in the relevant disciplines in order to keep collections and services up to date, analyse needs and propose improvements and adapted approaches Maintain regular interaction with academic stakeholders to identify evolving curriculum needs, new programmes, research priorities and resource requirements, and translate these into concrete collection and service developments Promote the libraries’ collections, resources and services through targeted communication, outreach, training and advocacy activities that emphasise added value to faculty and researchers Analyse usage data and user feedback to support evidence‑based decisions, prioritise activities based on needs and timeframe, and drive continuous improvement of collections and services Contribute to shaping and improving practices for cataloguing, classification, signage, collection maintenance and the organisation of documentary resources according to applicable standards Your profile Master’s degree or equivalent by work experience in Library, Information or Documentation Science; or a Master’s degree in a relevant discipline complemented by training or experience in information management At least 5 years of relevant professional experience, preferably in an academic or research library Strong experience in collection development, user support, reference services, information literacy and communication with academic users Good knowledge of library management systems, discovery tools, catalogues, databases and digital information resources Experience with collection development policies, acquisition workflows, budget monitoring, usage analysis and service improvement Ability to define, apply and improve standards, procedures, methods and tools related to library services and collection management Advanced digital literacy and good command of MS Office and professional library tools. Knowledge of Alma would be an advantage Language Requirements: Excellent command of English and French (C1); very good command of German and/or Luxembourgish (B2) would be considered an asset. We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 10 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Librarian specialist Job Reference: UOL08373 . About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Learning Centre (LLC), the University’s main library, supports students, researchers, staff and the wider public by providing documentary collections, information services and expertise that contribute to learning, teaching, and research. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-criminal-law-compliance-and-law-enforcement/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Criminal Law, Compliance and Law Enforcement",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08283 Your role The doctoral researcher will be working under the supervision of Professor Stanislaw Tosza. The doctoral researcher’s main task will be to prepare a doctoral thesis in the field of compliance and law enforcement. The thesis work will be undertaken at the University of Luxembourg but can also be jointly-supervised with another university. The suggested theme of the PhD is to explore the emerging role of artificial intelligence (AI) in corporate compliance programs implemented to prevent and detect crime. The candidate is welcome to suggest topics within this overarching theme. The doctoral candidate will contribute to the teaching activities. The doctoral researcher will benefit from being part of a research group comprising several doctoral and postdoctoral researchers working on related topics of criminal law and criminal procedure, enforcement, compliance, in particular focusing on new technologies. For more information concerning this position, please contact Prof. Stanislaw Tosza, email: stanislaw.tosza@uni.lu Your profile A Master’s Degree in criminal law, cyberlaw, law&tech, compliance, or EU law with the focus digital governance, or another one, which demonstrates interest in those disciplines Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken A detailed research proposal (2-4 pages) including a bibliography Name, contact information and current position of 1 referee who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system by August 15th 2026. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month, extendable to 48 months if required Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08283 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time) About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment.Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-economic-and-financial-history-with-focus-on-panama/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Economic and Financial History with Focus on Panama",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Luxembourg Center for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) Job reference UOL08484 Your role The doctoral researcher will work under the supervision of Professor Benoît Majerus within the ERC-funded project “Digital archaeology of shell companies: infrastructures of global connections and local networks (DIGSHELL)”. The project seeks to develop a comprehensive history of global tax networks by examining the emergence of multi-jurisdictional spaces in which nation-states, multinational corporations, local financial intermediaries, and international organizations interact to build, maintain, and govern global financial infrastructures. Building on a previous research initiative focused exclusively on Luxembourg, DIGSHELL adopts a broader international perspective through three additional case studies: Panama, Singapore and the British Virgin Islands (BVI). To facilitate the analysis of this extensive corpus, the project will explore advanced data analysis methods, visualization tools, and generative AI technologies, including Large Language Models (LLMs). The doctoral researcher will initially conduct preliminary research and review existing source materials in Luxembourg. This work will subsequently be complemented by extended research stays abroad, involving archival research, fieldwork, and interviews in the respective target country (Panama, Singapore, and the BVI/United Kingdom). Furthermore, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in the creation of networking opportunities, such as conferences and other events, and will disseminate results through scientific publications in well-ranked journals and conferences. For more information on DIGSHELL: https://www.uni.lu/c2dh-en/research-projects/digshell/ For further information on the position, please contact Prof. Benoît Majerus ( benoit.majerus@uni.lu ). Your profile Qualification : The candidate should have completed a master’s degree or equivalent in history, economics, political science, social science or a related field. Experience : The ideal candidate should have proven interest in the following topics: digital history, financial history, offshore studies, fiscal studies, network research Operational Language Requirements : Excellent command of English; good working knowledge of French is an asset. Excellent knowledge or full professional command of Spanish will be considered an advantage Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Name, contact information and current position of 1 referee who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate the person’s relationship to you A two-page project proposal (research question, sources, methodology) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08484 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) at the University of Luxembourg is an interdisciplinary research centre committed to high-quality research and public dissemination in the field of contemporary history with a particular focus on digital methods and tools.The C²DH’s ambition is to venture off the beaten track and find new ways of doing, teaching and presenting contemporary history of Luxembourg and the history of Europe in the 20th and 21st centuries. It serves as a catalyst for innovative and creative scholarship and new forms of public dissemination. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-ai-for-cybersecurity-systems-and-network-security/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in AI for Cybersecurity – Systems and Network Security",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07942 Your role Successful candidates will join the new Systems and Network Security Group led by Prof. Vincent Lenders . They will contribute to cutting-edge research in artificial intelligence for cybersecurity and perform the following tasks: Research: Conduct scientific research to advance the field of artificial intelligence on problems related to the cybersecurity of critical infrastructure Technology transfer: Work with industrial and governmental partners to transfer the group’s research results into functional prototypes and technology demonstrators for uses cases in cybersecurity automation. Education: Contribute in the teaching activities of the University’s Cybersecurity Master program and supervise Master students Dissemination: Present your research results at scientific conferences, journals and technology events. Your profile A MSc degree (or equivalent) in Cybersecurity, Computer Science Interest in security research and/or security engineering Ability to work in a multidisciplinary research environment Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Due to the specific requirements and constraints of the project, we are only able to consider applicants from EU EEA/EFTA countries, NATO Allied nations, and NATO Indo-Pacific Partners. Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Master thesis report 2 recommendation letters Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL07942 The yearly gross salary for every PhD at the UL is EUR 41976 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-advanced-wireless-optical-and-quantum-communications/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Advanced Wireless, Optical and Quantum Communications",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07983 Your role We look for Doctoral Researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in the 4 strategic research areas of SIGCOM, namely: i) Radio frequency transceiver design ; ii) Optical communications ; iii ) Quantum communications ; iv) System-level design and optimization . The related domains and topics for each of these research areas that we would like to attract excellent researchers to work on are the following: Radio frequency transceiver design Hardware & waveform design : Reconfigurable intelligent surfaces, flexible antennas, power amplifiers, 6G waveform design including Orthogonal-Time Frequency Space modulation and Discrete Fourier Transform-Spread-Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiplexing – DFT-s-OFDM Resource allocation and security design : Simultaneous wireless information and power transfer, physical layer design, joint source and channel coding, secure communications, jamming resilience techniques. Optical communications Photonics and free-space optics : Photonics, free-space optics arrays, PAT (pointing, acquisition, and tracking) for ISL Next-generation optical communications : SLIPT – Simultaneous light information and power transfer, AO – Adaptive optics, underwater optical communications, Li-Fi, OCC – Optical camera communications Quantum communications Computing & Networking : QuMIMO, Quantum Error Correction, Multi-partite systems, Q Network Coding, HQCNN – Hybrid Quantum-Classical Neural Networks Security & Logic : QRL – Quantum Reinforcement Learning, quantum computing, QKD – quantum key distribution, entanglement distribution System-level design and optimization AI & Intelligence : Agentic AI, Edge AI, information semantics e.g. for Earth Observation and Internet of Things, Telecom GPT, Open RAN/AI-RAN integration Infrastructure : MFSS – Multi-functional structures. ISAC – Integrated sensing and communications, Satellite swarms, unified terrestrial-non terrestrial networks, non-terrestrial network entanglement distribution The successful candidates are expected to disseminate their results through scientific publications and present them at well-known international conferences and workshops. Your profile M.Sc./M.Eng. Degree in telecommunication engineering, signal processing, machine learning or a closely related field in Electronic, Electrical and Computer Engineering The candidate should have at least 1 work published in prestigious journals and/or conferences, particularly Q1 journals and top-tier conference venues The candidate should have some knowledge and experience in some of the following topics/tools: 5G/6G wireless communications technologies Wireless Internet of Things technologies Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) Resource allocation and optimization Joint Communications and Sensing/PNT systems Network virtualization and network slicing MAC techniques/protocols for wireless systems Multi-antenna signal processing Graph signal processing Machine learning – supervised, unsupervised and reinforcement and tools such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, Keras and GreyCat Neuromorphic computing, spiking neural networks Deep learning – deep neural network, recurrent neural network, LSTM Optimization theory Stochastic geometry Strong programming skills in at least one of the following: MATLAB, Python, JULIA or C++ Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken A research statement (max. 1 page) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL07983 The yearly gross salary for every PhD at the UL is EUR 41976 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The Signal Processing and Communications (SIGCOM) research group of SnT conducts research aimed at designing, emulating and testing new high-performance systems for the future of mobile and satellite communications. Fields of applications range from 5G/6G telecommunications to satellite-based internet connectivity. For details, you may refer to the following: https://wwwen.uni.lu/snt/research/sigcom In addition, SIGCOM hosts the following experimental facilities: 6GSpaceLab: Real-world validation of advanced communication algorithms CommLab: Real-time wireless testbeds for DSP in satellite and terrestrial systems HybridNet Lab: Validation of large-scale autonomous and heterogeneous network orchestration QCI Lab: Quantum communication and QKD research across all network layers TelecomAI Lab: AI-based solutions for 5G/6G and satellite communications CSAT Lab: Design, fabrication, and measurement of advanced antenna technologies Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-computer-vision/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Computer Vision",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08044 Your role The successful candidates will join the Computer Vision, Machine Intelligence and Imaging (CVI2) research group, led by Prof. Djamila Aouada, to conduct research in Artificial Intelligence with a primary focus on Computer Vision, pattern recognition, and visual generative modeling. Multiple positions are available. CVI2 offers the opportunity to contribute to a diverse portfolio of projects, including collaborations with industrial partners as well as national and international academic initiatives. These projects span the full research and development lifecycle, requiring large-scale experimentation, real-time system implementation, data acquisition and curation, preprocessing, model training, validation, and rigorous performance evaluation. CVI2 is a dynamic, fast-growing research group composed of highly motivated, active members. The group benefits from advanced research infrastructure, including the Computer Vision Lab, equipped with state-of-the-art visual sensors and acquisition systems, and the Zero-G Lab, a unique facility designed to emulate proximity operations under space-like conditions. In addition, CVI2 provides high-performance GPU computing resources that support the design and training of advanced AI models. The research agenda of CVI2 focuses on cutting-edge topics such as 3D understanding and generation, media forensics, anomaly detection, multimodal learning with an emphasis on vision-language models, and computer vision applied to space applications. Key responsabilities: Develop novel research directions aligned with CVI2’s research priorities Propose and implementing innovative, concrete solutions and delivering impactful results Disseminate results through scientific publications and/or patents Provide support in setting up and running experiments Participate in proposal writing Develop and deploying real-time AI solutions Participate in organizing relevant workshops and demonstrations Participate in outreach activities to promote CVI2’s research activities and citizen science Your profile Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field Strong background in image/signal processing, and in particular, computer vision Strong programming skills in Python/C/C++/MATLAB Familiarity with machine learning and deep learning concepts Experience with at least one of the following deep learning frameworks: TensorFlow, PyTorch Experience with topics closely related or directly aligned with CVI2’s research priorities would be an asset Strong background in applied mathematics Capacity to adapt and thrive in a fast-paced and dynamic research environment Committed, collaborative, intellectually curious, and a strong critical thinker Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications, written in English, should be submitted online and should include: A full Curriculum Vitae Publication list, if any Transcripts of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Research statement and topics of particular interest to the candidate (300 words) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08044 The yearly gross salary for every PhD at the UL is EUR 41976 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-digital-business-information-systems-and-agentic-ai/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Digital Business, Information Systems, and Agentic AI",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08491 Your role Successful candidates will pursue a PhD degree in computer science and engineering with a focus on information systems while collaborating with our industry partner. More specifically, successful candidates will participate in a three-year industrial research project, “Agentic AI Platform for Reliable, Governed, and Customer-Centric AI in Regulated Energy Retail,” carried out with an industry partner in Luxembourg. The project aims to establish the scientific foundations for reliable, governed, and customer-centric agentic AI in the regulated European energy sector. In general, the candidate will perform the following tasks: Examining governance tensions that arise from the embedding of Agentic AI on an enterprise platform Exploring the implications of Agentic AI embedment in an enterprise platform from the perspective of (digital and data) sovereignty Examining the dynamics of human-agentic AI collaboration Understanding the security and privacy implications of Agentic AI (designs and) adoptions in the organiszational context Exploring the topic of customer delegation and engagement, e.g., understanding customers’ delegation preferences from interaction patterns In particular, they join a larger research team focused on Information Systems Research with experts in Digital Sovereignty, Agentic AI, and Energy Informatics and collaborate with team members working on related projects. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to investigate a broad range of research areas and design their own research portfolio. This allows them to align the skills they acquire while pursuing a doctorate with their personal goals and interests. Your profile The candidate should possess a MSc degree or equivalent in Information Systems, Business Administration/Management, Business Informatics, Computer Science, or related fields with a socio-technical background The ideal candidate should have interest and some knowledge and/or experience in several of the following topics (ordered by importance): Socio-technical or socio-economic study of technology adoption in organisations Digital sovereignty and/or cybersecurity Human-AI interaction, human-computer interaction and human factors Large language models and LLM-based agents Trustworthy AI, (platform) governance and regulation Experience working with industry and project management experience is desirable A collaborative team player with a willingness to conduct interdisciplinary research and a desire to make a personal impact within our research group Operational Language Requirements: Excellent command of English Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter including: A statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (why a doctoral program, why in Luxembourg, minimum 300 words) A statement on the candidate’s motivation for applying for this topic (minimum 300 words) Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08491 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Successful candidates will join the young, vibrant, and interdisciplinary FINATRAX Research Group, which builds bridges between business research and information systems engineering. The group conducts research on the application and the impact of technology on organisations in the private or public sector. Our team consists of international researchers with backgrounds in technology, law, management, economics, and other fields, united by a shared commitment to advancing sustainable technologies that benefit society. For more information, please visit our website: https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/finatrax/join-us/ Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-economic-and-financial-history-with-focus-on-singapore/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Economic and Financial History with Focus on Singapore",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Luxembourg Center for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) Job reference UOL08483 Your role The doctoral researcher will work under the supervision of Professor Benoît Majerus within the ERC-funded project “Digital archaeology of shell companies: infrastructures of global connections and local networks (DIGSHELL)”. The project seeks to develop a comprehensive history of global tax networks by examining the emergence of multi-jurisdictional spaces in which nation-states, multinational corporations, local financial intermediaries, and international organizations interact to build, maintain, and govern global financial infrastructures. Building on a previous research initiative focused exclusively on Luxembourg, DIGSHELL adopts a broader international perspective through three additional case studies: Panama, Singapore and the British Virgin Islands (BVI). To facilitate the analysis of this extensive corpus, the project will explore advanced data analysis methods, visualization tools, and generative AI technologies, including Large Language Models (LLMs). The doctoral researcher will initially conduct preliminary research and review existing source materials in Luxembourg. This work will subsequently be complemented by extended research stays abroad, involving archival research, fieldwork, and interviews in the respective target country (Panama, Singapore, and the BVI/United Kingdom). Furthermore, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in the creation of networking opportunities, such as conferences and other events, and will disseminate results through scientific publications in well-ranked journals and conferences. For more information on DIGSHELL: https://www.uni.lu/c2dh-en/research-projects/digshell/ For further information on the position, please contact Prof. Benoît Majerus ( benoit.majerus@uni.lu ). Your profile Qualification : The candidate should have completed a master’s degree or equivalent in history, economics, political science, social science or a related field Experience : The ideal candidate should have proven interest in the following topics: digital history, financial history, offshore studies, fiscal studies, network research Operational Language Requirements : Excellent command of English; good working knowledge of French is an asset. Basic knowledge of Mandarin is considered an advantage Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Name, contact information and current position of 1 referee who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate the person’s relationship to you A two-page project proposal (research question, sources, methodology) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Part Time 38.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08483 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH) at the University of Luxembourg is an interdisciplinary research centre committed to high-quality research and public dissemination in the field of contemporary history with a particular focus on digital methods and tools.The C²DH’s ambition is to venture off the beaten track and find new ways of doing, teaching and presenting contemporary history of Luxembourg and the history of Europe in the 20th and 21st centuries. It serves as a catalyst for innovative and creative scholarship and new forms of public dissemination. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-economics/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Economics",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08284 Your role The doctoral researcher will be working under the supervision of Professor Michel Beine. The doctoral researcher’s main task will be to prepare a doctoral thesis in the field of the economic analysis of migration. The thesis work will be undertaken at the University of Luxembourg but can also be jointly-supervised with another university. The suggested theme of the PhD is on the economic analysis of the determinants and consequences of human mobility. The candidate is, however, welcome to suggest any other topic within the overarching project theme. The doctoral candidate will contribute to the teaching of classes ranging from one to three hours per week, of small group teachings and tutorials. The doctoral researcher will benefit from being part of large research group comprising several PhDs and Postdoctoral Researchers working on related topics in the filed of the economic analysis of globalization. Being part of the project will allow the doctoral researcher to enhance one’s knowledge-base and experience; working on the various aspects of the project will not only strengthen the academic profile, but also give the candidate an access to (and the chance to critically engage with) some of the most renowned experts in the field. For more information concerning this position, please contact Prof Michel Beine; email: Michel.beine@uni.lu Your profile A Master’s Degree in Economics Strong skills in econometrics and data analysis, with a strong emphasis on causal inference techniques Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Master’s degree title and awarding university The name, current position and relationship to the applicant, of one referee Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. To ensure full consideration, candidates should apply ONLINE formally through the HR system by 15/09/2026. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month, extendable to 48 months if required Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08284 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment.Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. Apply online Location Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-insolvency-law/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Insolvency Law",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08245 Your role The doctoral researcher will be working under the supervision of Professor Mastrullo. The doctoral researcher’s main task will be to prepare a doctoral thesis in the field of insolvency law or company law, preferably with a comparative, international and/or European perspective, in French or English language. The thesis work will be undertaken at the University of Luxembourg but can also be jointly-supervised with another university. The suggested themes of the PhD is The protection of creditors in European insolvency law or Le droit applicable aux pactes d’actionnaires internationaux. The candidate is, however, welcome to suggest any other topic within the overarching project theme. The doctoral candidate will contribute to the teaching of classes ranging from one to three hours per week, of small group teachings and tutorials. The doctoral researcher will benefit from being part of large research group comprising several PhDs and Postdoctoral Researchers working on related topics of business law (insolvency, company, banking or financial law). Being part of the project will allow the doctoral researcher to enhance the knowledge-base and experience; working on the various aspects of the project will not only strengthen the candidate’s academic profile, but also give the person access to (and the chance to critically engage with) some of the most renowned experts in the field. For more information concerning this position, please contact Prof. Mastrullo, email: thomas.mastrullo@uni.lu Your profile A Master’s Degree in business law or private international law Demonstrated interest in business law, EU law and international law Language Requirements: Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Name, contact information and current position of 1 referee who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate the person’s relationship to you Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month, extendable to 48 months if required Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08245 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 43445 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment.Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-on-the-legal-status-of-ethical-hackers/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher on the Legal Status of Ethical Hackers",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08453 Your role The doctoral researcher will be working under the supervision of Professor Niovi Vavoula, Chair in Cyber Policy, with Dr Sergio Coronado (Adjunct Professor at the UL and Luxembourg Tech School A.s.b.l.) being a member of the PhD Committee. The thesis work will be undertaken at the University of Luxembourg. The doctoral researcher’s main task will be to prepare a doctoral thesis on the criminal (non-)protection of casual ethical hackers. In particular, the doctoral researcher will be mapping, evaluating and comparing EU and national legislation of EU Member States and NATO states, that are parties to the Budapest Convention, concerning the protection (or non-protection) of ethical hackers. The doctoral candidate will contribute to the compilation of national (Luxembourg) legislation, the assessment of legislative exemptions, the identification of good models and practices, the creation of an interactive map of national laws, and to the teaching of classes ranging from one to three hours per week, of small group teachings and tutorials. The doctoral researcher will benefit from being part of large research group comprising several PhDs and Postdoctoral Researchers working on related topics of cyber policy and criminal law. Being part of the SAFEHACK project will allow the doctoral researcher to enhance one’s knowledge-base and experience; working on the various aspects of the project will not only strengthen one’s academic profile, but also give the person access to (and the chance to critically engage with) some of the most renowned experts in the field. About the project: The SAFEHACK project aims to map the legal and policy framework on onboarding casual ethical hackers in, and by engaging with relevant stakeholders to propose draft legislation and policy recommendations at national (Luxembourg), EU and international level aimed at providing a protective framework to ethical hackers. A harmonised legal and policy framework would better support government and critical sectors’ defensive efforts under regulated conditions and an overall safe environment for ethical hackers. For more information concerning this position, please contact Prof. Niovi Vavoula, email: Niovi.vavoula@uni.lu . Your profile We are looking for a candidate with demonstrated interest in criminal law (EU and international) and cybersecurity, including cybercrime, cybersecurity of critical infrastructure, cyber defence and cyber sovereignty. In particular, the following requirements apply : A Master’s Degree in Law, particularly in criminal law or IT law Operational Language Requirements: Excellent command in English (C1) is required. Good working knowledge (B1) of a second language, French in particular, and possibly a third language, German in particular, will be considered an advantage Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae, including list of publications and copies thereof, if applicable Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Names, contact information and current position of up to 3 referees who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate their relationship to you A 5-page research proposal Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08453 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment.Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. The Department of Law of the Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance of the University of Luxembourg is looking for a PhD candidate to conduct research on the protection of ethical hackers through criminal law, in the context of the SAFEHACK (Safe Access Framework for Ethical HACKers) project, funded by the University of Luxembourg Cyber Research Hub. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/doctoral-researcher-in-in-entrepreneurship/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in in Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08311 Your role The doctoral researcher will prepare a cumulative, paper-based doctoral thesis in entrepreneurship under the supervision of Prof. Christian Fisch, with the goal of publishing in leading international entrepreneurship and management journals. The thesis topic is open within EINT’s research areas. Other topics in entrepreneurship and innovation are also welcome if the applicant has a strong interest and a promising idea. The thesis should be be quantitative and empirical, normally using large-scale datasets, statistical programming, and econometric methods. Other methods may be used as a complement where clearly justified, but this is not a primarily qualitative research position. Applicants should apply only if they can demonstrate strong quantitative preparation and relevant empirical research experience. A general interest in sustainability, finance, entrepreneurship, or AI without the required methodological background is not sufficient. The successful candidate will join a team of doctoral and postdoctoral researchers and benefit from EINT’s ongoing projects, methodological expertise, and data infrastructure while taking substantial responsibility for developing and executing their own research. The doctoral researcher’s key responsibilities include: Developing original, theoretically grounded research questions Identifying and constructing appropriate empirical datasets Conducting quantitative analyses using reproducible research workflows Developing research projects from initial idea through manuscript preparation, revision and submission Presenting research at top international conferences and building a professional network in the entrepreneurship research community Completing the training program of the Doctoral School in Economics, Finance and Management Your profile A completed or nearly completed Master’s degree or equivalent qualification in management, business administration, economics, finance, or a related field Advanced university-level training in empirical research methods, statistics, econometrics, or a closely related field Practical experience conducting empirical analysis with statistical software such as Stata, R, or Python A proactive and independent working style, with strong communication skills and high curiosity A genuine interest in developing independent research in entrepreneurship Operational Language Requirements: Excellent command in English (C1) is required In exceptional cases, applicants with a Master’s degree in computer science, data science, or a closely related technical field may also be considered. Such candidates must demonstrate a strong interest in entrepreneurship research and explain convincingly how their technical background can be applied to theoretically grounded research questions in sustainable entrepreneurship, entrepreneurial finance, or entrepreneurship and AI. Academic Eligibility (Thesis): Applicants must demonstrate at least B2-level proficiency in the language of their thesis. For details and accepted certificates, please visit the Application for admission – Doctoral Candidates . We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter presenting your motivation for this doctoral thesis topic, and explaining how your qualifications and aspirations align with its academic focus Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Master’s thesis or, if not yet completed, a draft or a comparable piece of independent written work (e.g., a seminar paper) Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month (extendable to a maximum of 48 months) Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Doctoral Researcher Job Reference: UOL08311 The yearly gross salary for every Doctoral researcher at the UL is EUR 44531 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The successful candidate will join the Entrepreneurship, Innovation, and New Technology (EINT) research group, led by Prof. Christian Fisch. EINT conducts interdisciplinary research on entrepreneurship and innovation, with a particular focus on the areas of entrepreneurial finance (e.g., venture capital, business angels, crowdfunding), sustainable entrepreneurship (e.g., climate change, sustainability certifications, impact investing), and entrepreneurship and AI (e.g., AI adoption by entrepreneurs, AI as a method in entrepreneurship research). Across these areas, the group studies novel phenomena using large-scale data and quantitative methods. EINT aims to realize impact through publications in top journals, presentations at leading international conferences, and close collaboration with industry and policy partners. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/project-officer-for-study-programmes-in-health-sciences/": {
      "title": "Project Officer for Study Programmes in Health Sciences",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Limited contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08517 Your role The Project Officer will play an essential role in developing the learning experiences of Health Professionals, by supporting the coordination and delivery of the University’s Study Programmes in Health Sciences. Working under the accountability of the Programme Directors and project owners,the person will coordinate activities across the academic year and project life cycles, and help ensure that the set objectives are achieved. The candidate will work closely with academic and administrative teams, internal services, healthcare partners, and other stakeholders. Main responsibilities: Contribute to Study Programme retro-planning, project plans, timelines and budget follow-up for the allocated Study Programme(s) in Health Sciences Coordinate the execution of Health Sciences Study Programmes and associated projects with Programme Directors, project owners and relevant stakeholders Monitor deliverables, milestones, risks and key performance indicators throughout the academic year and/or project life cycle Organise meetings, task forces and seminars, prepare supporting documents, draft minutes and reports, and follow up on decisions and actions Act as an interface for internal and external stakeholders and facilitate clear communication Build and maintain relationships with healthcare and education partners, suppliers and other relevant organisations Compile and analyse information and prepare periodic and ad hoc reports, briefings and presentations Provide Line Manager, Study Programme Directors, project owners and associated teams, with regular status updates Maintain accurate Study Programme records in line with agreed requirements and University guideline Your profile Master’s degree or equivalent by work experience A minimum of 4 to 6 years of relevant working experience Knowledge of the Luxembourgish Healthcare sector or the uni.lu education environment is a strong advantage Management certification is an added value Proficient use of MS Office tools: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams Familiarity with MS Planner and agile management practices Demonstrated initiative and ability to manage multiple tasks independently A team player with a diplomatic, friendly, and service-oriented attitude Reliable, proactive, and flexible in responding to changing priorities Excellent command of English and French is required. Good working knowledge of Luxembourgish or German is a strong asset We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Project officer Job Reference: UOL08517 . About the FSTM The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine. Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-software-engineering-for-cyber-physical-systems/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Software Engineering for Cyber-Physical Systems",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08232 Your role Carrying out research in the predefined areas Implementing proof-of-concept solutions Empirically evaluating the proposed solutions and tools Disseminating results through scientific publications Preparing and organizing project meetings, including off-site meetings in Vienna Providing guidance to PhD, master, and bachelor students Organizing relevant workshops and demonstrations Preparing project deliverables and reports Presenting results in well-known international conferences and workshops Contributing to the acquisition of research funding Managing and contributing to national and international research projects We offer an attractive research associate position in the context of the FREELY (Frequency-enhanced verification and validation of CPS) project, funded by the Luxembourg National Research Fund (FNR). The project aims to develop methods and techniques for enabling the use of frequency-based specifications in V&V activities for cyber-physical systems. The project will be carried out in collaboration with the TrustCPS group of TU Wien (led by prof. Ezio Bartocci). The successful candidate will join the SVV research group headed by Prof. Domenico Bianculli and will report to the latter (PI of the project). The team focuses on the development and design of reliable, safe, and secure software systems, carrying out both upstream activities such as requirements quality assurance and architecture analysis, as well as downstream verification & validation activities, such as software testing and runtime verification. For further information, you may refer to https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/svv Your profile We are looking for a motivated candidate who can work independently and efficiently, is proactive in solving problems, and has strong analytical skills. The candidate should be interested in working in an international team with a multi-disciplinary set of backgrounds, where sharing resources and teamwork is essential. Most importantly, the candidate should be curiosity driven and willing to constantly learn new things! Qualification: PhD degree in Computer Science, Informatics, Software Engineering, or a related field. Experience: Knowledge (supported by a sound publication track record in relevant international conferences and top journals) of one or more of the following topics: Software Verification and Validation Temporal logics Formal methods Background in any of the following topics: Runtime verification and monitoring Specification inference Testing of Cyber-physical systems Fault localization and failure explanation Machine learning for software verification Proficiency in a major programming language will be considered as an asset Language Skills: Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English are required. We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Research statement Contact information for 3 referees List of publications Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 18 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08232 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-statistical-physics-of-active-matter/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Statistical Physics of Active Matter",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08362 Your role The project aims to develop novel analytical and numerical techniques to study collective states in active matter. Depending on the candidate’s profile and interests, the research can involve various aspects of the modeling and the optimal control of active systems. The candidate is also expected to take part in the scientific activities organized within Physics of Active Matter group and the Department of Physics and Materials Science, such as seminars, colloquia, and summer schools. Your profile PhD in Theoretical Physics Excellent analytical and numerical skills Solid knowledge of Statistical Physics Proficient in English (C1) We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Degree certificates and transcripts of university-level courses, including grades 2 recommendation letters Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08362 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About the FSTM The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine. Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and environment we live in. The selected candidate will join the group Physics of Active Matter at the University of Luxembourg: https://efodorphysics.github Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-translational-cancer-bioinformatics/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Translational Cancer Bioinformatics",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08447 Your role We seek a postdoctoral fellow with a strong background in bioinformatics and cancer biology and a passion for investigating the role of the tumor microenvironment, in particular CAF-driven epithelial plasticity, using advanced experimental models. The primary research focus will be to define how fibroblasts from healthy colon tissue transition into distinct CAF subtypes and how these subtypes regulate epithelial plasticity and immune responses, promoting tumor progression and therapy resistance. This work will integrate spatial transcriptomics, advanced co-culture organoid assays, and in vivo models to decode the mechanisms underlying CAF-driven CRC evolution. Access to single cell RNA sequencing and spatial transcriptomics data from active clinical trials through the group of Prof Tejpar will put the postdoc in an ideal position to understand how the stromal interactions change under current novel treatments and could be harnessed as future therapies. Main responsibilities: Coordinate experiments for the TARGET-SEQ project Conduct bioinformatics analysis and implement new tools Collect, interpret, and analyse research related data and results Ensure proper scientific documentation, e.g. protocols, reports Document performed experiments and analyses in a lab book Participate and present obtained data in bi-monthly consortium meetings Present the data in scientific publications Contribute to general tasks in the laboratory The postdoctoral fellow will focus on applying innovative bioinformatics approaches to human-relevant models and unique patient-derived tissue cohorts from colorectal cancer. The aim is to dissect the tumor “ecosystem” with a particular emphasis on epithelial cells, cancer-associated fibroblasts (CAFs) and immune cells, and to comprehensively profile their phenotypic and functional heterogeneity, lineage plasticity, and evolutionary dynamics. These insights will help advance our understanding of colorectal cancer development, progression, and therapeutic response. For all in vitro and in vivo experiments, the Postdoctoral Fellow will be supported by a dedicated technician, who will be recruited concurrently for this project. The position will be jointly based in the Letellier and Tejpar laboratories, with close collaboration across research groups and clinical partners. For further information, please contact Prof. Dr. Elisabeth Letellier: Elisabeth.letellier@uni.lu Your profile PhD in Biological Sciences, Data Science, Computational Biology, or a related discipline Preferably with prior professional experience as a Postdoctoral Researcher Strong computational background with proficiency in R and at least one additional scripting language, e.g., Python Solid knowledge of biostatistics Experience with single-cell sequencing data and preferentially with spatial omics Working in high-performance computing environments is highly preferred Good understanding of cancer biology, immunology, cell biology, and molecular biology is required Proven track record of peer-reviewed publications Strong organizational skills Excellent command in English (C1) is required We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications The name and contact details of at least two referees Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08447 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine.Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. Our collaborative group, composed of the MDM group at the University of Luxembourg, led by Prof. Letellier and the laboratory of Prof. Tejpar at the KU Leuven, investigates stromal–epithelial crosstalk in colorectal cancer (CRC) initiation, progression and therapy resistance. Using state-of-the-art single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNAseq) and spatial transcriptomics on CRC patient samples, we have identified novel epithelial cell states and distinct cancer-associated fibroblast (CAF) subpopulations. The postdoctoral fellow will work jointly between the University of Luxembourg and the KU Leuven, benefiting from a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary environment, and contributing to the TARGET-SEC project’s overarching goal of identifying novel therapeutic strategies targeting pro-tumorigenic stroma–epithelial interactions in CRC. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-information-systems-and-artificial-intelligence/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Information Systems and Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08312 Your role Conduct cutting-edge research in areas of interest to FINATRAX, particularly linking information systems and artificial intelligence: Investigating the design knowledge of developing AI-based information systems, such as AI-enabled engagement e.g., agentic AI and AI-enabled insight generation e.g., machine learning analytics in both individual and organizational contexts Exploring Human-AI collaboration Designing, prototyping and implementing AI-based information systems that address pressing challenges in private and public sectors Evaluating the impacts of AI-based information systems using both quantitative and qualitative approaches Investigating and applying AI as a research method in IS e.g., computationally intensive theory construction Prepare research proposals to attract industry partnerships as well as national and European grant projects Manage research projects and prepare project deliverables in collaboration with our industry partners Disseminate results through scientific publications, aiming for the best-ranked outlets Communicate and work with stakeholders in government: ministries, regulators, government-run start-up incubators and companies Mentor and supervise PhD students, providing guidance and support in their research endeavors The group conducts research on the application and the impact of technology on organisations in the private or public sector. Our team consists of international researchers with backgrounds in technology, law, management, economics, and other fields, united by a shared commitment to advancing sustainable technologies that benefit society. For more information, please visit our website: https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/finatrax/research/ For further information, please contact Muriel-Larissa FRANK ( muriel.frank@uni.lu) , Antragama Ewa ABBAS ( antragama.abbas@uni.lu ), and Gilbert FRIDGEN ( gilbert.fridgen@uni.lu ). Your profile PhD degree in Information Systems, Business Informatics, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering, Human-AI Interaction, or a related field Proficiency in research methods commonly used in IS research, such as design science research Strong interest in publishing in high-ranked journals such as the Association for Information Systems Senior Scholars’ List of Premier Journals and in related outlets like Business & Information Systems Engineering, Electronic Markets, and in IS conferences like ICIS, ECIS, and DESRIST, CaiSE Proven track record of publishing research papers in the aforementioned conferences and in top-tier IS journals Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English are required. Knowledge of French, German, and Luxembourgish is not required. We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing: A research statement and a list of topics of particular interest to the candidate (250 words), followed by a concrete research agenda of planned research activities that are aligned with the topics covered by FINATRAX and ideally target the Information Systems discipline (max 500 words). Please discuss research questions, including methods, theoretical lenses (if any), and targeted outlets (conferences/journals) A statement on the candidate’s personal motivation for applying (250 words) A strategy for the acquisition of research grants and industry partnerships (250 words) PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08312 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-machine-learning-and-surrogate-modelling/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Machine Learning and Surrogate Modelling",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07986 Your role This position sits at the interface of machine learning, uncertainty quantification and computational biomechanics. You will work within the Legato group and in close collaboration with ARSPECTRA to design and deploy probabilistic surrogate models that run on ARSPECTRA’s devices and provide robust, real-time guidance to neurosurgeons. Key Responsabilities: Design and implement Bayesian graph neural networks and convolutional neural networks as surrogates for high-fidelity biomechanical models Quantify and propagate uncertainty, and develop strategies for model selection and switching in real time Integrate surrogate models with physics-based solvers, e.g. SOFA, FEniCSx, SOniCS, and clinical or phantom data Deploy models on ARSPECTRA hardware, including optimisation for embedded and GPU platforms. Collaborate with ARSPECTRA engineers and surgeons to create a complete AR guidance pipeline : tracking, SLAM, gaze, user interface Your profile PhD in machine learning, computational mechanics, computer science, applied mathematics or similar Strong experience with deep learning, e.g. PyTorch, JAX, TensorFlow, and probabilistic methods Familiarity with graph neural networks, convolutional architectures and surrogate modelling for physical systems Solid understanding of PDE-based models or the motivation to acquire this knowledge Experience with real-time or edge deployment (CUDA, ONNX, TensorRT, FPGA) is an advantage Ability to work across disciplines – mechanics, ML, hardware, medicine We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL07986 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 85176 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-number-theory-arithmetic-geometry/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Number Theory, Representation Theory & Arithmetic Geometry",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08482 Your role Conduct research on topics related to the research interests of the group; an interest in the Langlands Program (broadly interpreted), p-adic Hodge theory, etc. would be considered an asset Participate in the scientific activities of the Department of Mathematics Contribution to the teaching mission of the Department of mathematics for up to 45 hours per year Contribution to the outreach activities of the Department of mathematics If you have questions regarding the position, please contact Prof. Yujie Xu at xu.yujie@columbia.edu . Administrative questions should be directed to math.office@uni.lu . Your profile PhD of high quality in mathematics and an outstanding research record, relative to career stage, in a relevant research area Interest in Number Theory, Representation Theory, Arithmetic Geometry or related areas Excellent command in English is required. Good working knowledge of French would be desirable but not required We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date. You can also include a copy of your PhD thesis, or an extended abstract if the thesis is not yet completed Research Statement List of publications The names and email addresses of at least 3 references (for research) who can be contacted by us to provide a reference letter on the candidate’s research abilities; candidates can choose to submit an additional reference letter regarding teaching, but this is optional Any other relevant documents, e.g. Teaching Statement, Teaching Evaluations, Outreach Statement Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Applicants are encouraged to apply by October 20th, 2026. Late applications may continue to be reviewed until the position has been filled. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month, renewable up to 4 years subject to agreement with the Professor Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Teaching duties of up to 45 hours per year (60 teaching units of 45min/unit) Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08482 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). In addition, there is a generous budget for travel and inviting collaborators for postdoctoral researchers. About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine.Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. The Department of Mathematics (DMATH) of the University of Luxembourg invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position to start in September 2027. The researcher will be a part of the research group of Prof. Yujie Xu in Number Theory, Representation Theory and/or Arithmetic Geometry, broadly interpreted. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-cancer-microbiome/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Cancer & Microbiome",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08422 Your role Participate in experiments within different microbiome and cancer related project Collect, interpret, and analyse research related data and results Ensure proper scientific documentation, e.g. protocols, reports Document performed experiments and analyses in a lab book Participate and present obtained data in meeting Participate in the generation of scientific reports Contribute to general tasks in the laboratory Contribute to cooperation with other research organisations The activities can be subject to changes or adaptations if required by the project, the structure or the needs of the laboratory. For further information, please contact Prof. Dr. Elisabeth Letellier Elisabeth.letellier@uni.lu Your profile Master’s degree in Biological Sciences or related discipline Previous professional experience as a research technician or research and development engineer Experience with conducting animal/in-vivo experiments is required Experience in cell culture techniques, if possible, in 3D cell culture models (organoids, spheroids) Experience in molecular biology techniques such as real-time PCR, FACS analysis, Western blotting, imaging techniques are considered an advantage Skills in written and spoken English is required (C1), knowledge in German or French (B1) is an asset We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08422 . About the FSTM The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine. Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-historical-economic-data/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Historical Economic Data",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08509 Your role Locating and obtaining historical statistical sources that exist only in print or as scans, such as official statistical yearbooks, government publications, monographs and archival records, many of them in languages other than English Consulting volumes in libraries and archives, including occasional trips abroad, e.g. to the United Kingdom, when a source cannot be accessed remotely, and handling registration and access requests with statistical offices and data archives Transcribing statistical tables from printed volumes and scans, and checking every figure against the original page Documenting each series, e.g. source, coverage, units, territory and method of compilation, and maintaining the project’s data files under version control, in preparation for their public release Coordinating the data work of master students and supporting the project’s doctoral researcher The Research and Development Specialist will work under the supervision of Prof. Julien Pénasse. Your profile Master’s degree in economic history or a closely related field, and at least two years of research experience with historical data Precision with numbers and careful documentation of sources Willingness to travel for short library and archive visits Excellent command of English is required The following will be considered an advantage: Experience with historical sources, such as archival research or the compilation of historical statistics Good working knowledge of German, French, Dutch, Italian, Spanish or a Scandinavian language Experience processing data and programming in any language (for example Python, R, MATLAB or Julia), including version control with Git Experience using AI assistants such as Claude or Codex We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 10 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08509 . About the FDEF The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment. Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-quantum-networking/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Quantum Networking",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08382 Your role The successful candidate is expected to assume a role in the design and development of software for quantum networking, in accordance with ongoing European initiatives and projects. The candidate will play a central role in the engineering of software components for QKD networks, including key management, network control and orchestration, and the integration of quantum and classical security mechanisms. Responsibilities encompass the full software lifecycle, from requirements analysis, architecture and design through implementation, testing and deployment, following sound software engineering practices in a collaborative development environment. The candidate is also expected to support PhD candidates and researchers in their development and prototyping activities. English is the working language of this international laboratory, which is engaged in several European and international projects and conducts cutting-edge research in close collaboration with academic and industry partners. Your profile The candidate is expected to hold, or be close to completing, a master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Physics, Photonics, Telecommunications, Quantum Technologies, or a related discipline, with a focus on software development and a solid grounding in networking and applied cryptography. Candidates without a PhD are eligible for this Research and Development position. Required qualifications: Strong software development skills in two or more of Python, Rust, C and C++ Proficiency with version control systems (Git) and collaborative development workflows Knowledge of software engineering best practices: modular design, automated testing, continuous integration, code review, and documentation Working knowledge of networking fundamentals: TCP/IP, sockets, secure communication protocols Notions of cryptography and a keen interest in quantum and post-quantum security: QKD, key management, PQC, are highly needed Notions of software-defined networking (SDN) and network function virtualization (NFV) paradigms Ability to work autonomously and as part of a multidisciplinary, internationally distributed team Fluent written and verbal communication skills in English are mandatory If you want to know more about the role, please feel free to contact Dr. Seid Koudia at seid.koudia@uni.lu and Dr. Juan Carlos Hernandez-Hernandez at juancarlos.hernandez@uni.lu We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. The University of Luxembourg is committed to achieving gender parity among its staff. Should candidates present equivalent profiles, preference will be given to female candidates in all departments where gender parity is not yet achieved. The University of Luxembourg embraces inclusion and diversity as key values. We are fully committed to removing any discriminatory barrier related to gender, and not only, in recruitment and career progression of our staff. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08382 . About the SnT The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services. We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The Signal Processing and Communications (SigCom) research group of SnT, headed by Prof. Symeon Chatzinotas, focuses on wireless/satellite communications and networking. The research areas focus on the formulation, modeling, design, and analysis of future 6G communication networks that are capable of supporting new services for digital ecosystems. Use cases of interest include Security and Efficient Wireless Communication Solutions, IoT verticals, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Integrated Satellite-Space-Terrestrial Networks, Quantum Communications and Quantum Information Networks, Spectrum Management and Coexistence, Tactile Internet, Earth Observation, and Autonomous Transportation. As far as technical enablers are concerned, we leverage expertise in advanced technologies including semantic/task-oriented data processing, signal processing, and network resource management to improve the performance of future wireless communication systems. Finally, due to the large-scale nature, complexity, and heterogeneity of 6G networks, we use tools such as artificial intelligence/machine learning, quantum computing, graph theory, graph-signal processing, and convex/non-convex optimization. Furthermore, our activities are experimentally driven and supported by the COMMLab, the 6GSPACE Lab, the HybridNetLab, the QCILab, our SW Simulators, and our facilities. For further information, you may refer to https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/sigcom/ . Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-on-the-policy-framework-for-onboarding-ethical-hackers/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher on the Policy Framework for Onboarding Ethical Hackers",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Weicker Building Organisation Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) Job reference UOL08451 Your role Conduct research and contribute to other activities falling into the scope of the research projects, in particular: drafting research papers, prepare the scientific materials of project meetings; contributing to project events’ organisation Conduct own research in the related topics, publish articles in scientific reviews and contribute to conferences Assist with teaching activities, one to three hours a week and contribute to tutoring students Contribute to preparing further research proposals Offer research assistance and coordinate young researchers working in the same field About the project: The SAFEHACK project aims to map the legal and policy framework on onboarding casual ethical hackers in, and by engaging with relevant stakeholders to propose draft legislation and policy recommendations at national (Luxembourg), EU and international level aimed at providing a protective framework to ethical hackers. A harmonised legal and policy framework would better support government and critical sectors’ defensive efforts under regulated conditions and an overall safe environment for ethical hackers. For more information concerning this position, please contact Prof. Niovi Vavoula, email: Niovi.vavoula@uni.lu. Your profile We are looking for a candidate with a PhD in Law, with a specialisation in Cybersecurity law / IT law / Law & Technology. Candidates without a background in Law are not eligible for this position. In particular, the following requirements apply: Strong interest in cyber law and policy, including cybersecurity, cyber defence, cybercrime and cyber sovereignty, as well as in interdisciplinary research; academic or practical experience in topics linked to the research will be considered an advantage Proven ability to autonomously conduct research at a post-doctoral level Good IT skills Excellent command in English (C1) is required. Good working knowledge (B1) of a second language, preferably French or German, would be considered an advantage We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae with a complete bibliography of published works Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Degree certificates and transcripts of university-level courses, including grades Names, contact information and current position of up to 3 referees who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate their relationship to you List of publications, including open-access links where available Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Weicker Building Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08451 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance (FDEF) at the University of Luxembourg offers a unique academic and research environment.Rooted in Luxembourg but with a European and international outlook, teaching and research benefit from the proximity of the European institutions, Luxembourg’s leading international financial centre and its vibrant business community. Institutional and private sector partnerships, sponsored Chairs and a growing network of international partner universities make the FDEF a dynamic academic hub at the heart of Europe. The Department of Law of the Faculty of Law, Economics and Finance of the University of Luxembourg is looking for a Postdoctoral researcher to conduct research on national policies (CVD policies and bug bounty programmes in the EU) to onboard ethical hackers, in the context of the SAFEHACK (Safe Access Framework for Ethical HACKers) project. The postdoctoral researcher will be working under the supervision of Professor Niovi Vavoula, Chair in Cyber Policy, with Dr Sergio Coronado (Adjunct Professor at the U and Luxembourg Tech School A.s.b.l.). Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-cognitive-psychology/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Cognitive Psychology",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) Job reference UOL07494 Your role The Postdoctoral researcher will be working in the Institute for Lifelong Learning and Guidance, within the Department of Education and Social Work. The person will be part of a dynamic organisational context of a growing, globally connected research university. The postdoctoral researcher will collaborate closely with Prof. Dr Claude Houssemand ( https://wwwen.uni.lu/forschung/fhse/desw/people/claude_houssemand/ ) on topics related to cognitive differential psychology, especially cognitive strategies in visuo-spatial tasks. Key Responsibilities: Collaboration and support of research and administrative tasks in the field of psychology, education and guidance Self-organised and collaborative research Application for and coordination of (international) third-party funding Publications in peer-reviewed journals Innovative teaching Independent supervision of students and doctoral researchers Transfer of relevant research results to various communities and a wider public Academic self-administration (Institute, Department and Faculty) For questions and further information, please contact claude.houssemand@uni.lu Your profile PhD in psychology, with a focus on at least one of the below areas: Cognitive psychology Differential psychology Neuropsychology Evaluation and Assessment Methodology and Statistics Interest in psychological and cognitive science issues and ambition to advance one of the aforementioned subject areas Fluency in English and French is required; good command of Luxembourgish and / or German is considered an asset Training and experience in quantitative empirical methods Good command of multivariate and complex statistical methods International publications in peer-reviewed journals and / or book publications as well as alternative approaches to research communication/ data management Innovative teaching experience We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications in English should include: Cover letter explaining your motivation Curriculum Vitae (including your contact address, work experience) Copies of diplomas List of publications Summary of recent research and projects Sketch of planned research and publication activities (2 pages each) Contact information of at least two referees Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Candidates should apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Planned Start Date: beginning of May 2026 Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL07494 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 85176 (full time). About the FHSE The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) at the University of Luxembourg brings together expertise from the humanities, linguistics, cognitive sciences, social and educational sciences. People from across 20 disciplines are working within the Faculty. Along with the disciplinary approach a very ambitious interdisciplinary research culture has been developed. The faculty’s research and teaching focuses on social, economic, political and educational issues with the common goal of contributing to an inclusive, open and resourceful society. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-educational-sciences/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Educational Sciences",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) Job reference UOL07935 Your role The Postdoctoral researcher will be a member of the Institute for Teaching and Learning within the Department of Education and Social Work at the University of Luxembourg. The person will be part of a team in the dynamic organisational context of a growing, globally connected research university. The postdoctoral researcher will work with Professor Dr Janne Fengler on gaining understandings of contexts and processes of learning and teaching. The ideal candidate has substantive interest in related issues, advanced methodological training (qualitative and / or quantitative) and would like to contribute to an international and multilingual team. Responsibilities: Content-related and organizational support for the professorship Project-related and independent research at the interface of education and social work Application for and organisation of third-party funding Publications in peer-reviewed journals, preferably in English and / or German Teaching in the study program Bachelor en Formation Pédagogique and possibly further study programs at the Department of Education and Social Work Independent supervision of students and doctoral candidates Support in the further development of the Bachelor en Formation Pédagogique program and in the expansion of networks with stakeholders and partners Transfer of relevant results to various communities from science and politics to a broader public Academic self-administration – Institute, Department and Faculty For questions and further information, please contact Prof. Dr Janne Fengler at janne.fengler@uni.lu Your profile Excellent PhD in Educational Sciences, preferably with reference to one of the following subject areas: experiential education / outdoor education educational instruction / didactics and methodology / teaching-learning-research university didactics / future skills pedagogical professionalisation / teacher education victimology / social inequality / social exclusion / social participation Interest in educational science issues, strong personal commitment and ambition to advance one of the aforementioned subject areas Fluency in English and either German or French is required, the respective other language and / or Luxembourgish will be considered an asset Interest in empirical social research, excellent command of quantitative and / or qualitative empirical methods; openness to mixed methods research International publications in peer-reviewed journals and / or book publications Demonstrated teaching experience Demonstrated project management skills Ability and willingness to work both independently and as part of a team Ability to meet deadlines and a positive, proactive attitude to balance research, teaching and administrative activities We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objectives Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Copies of diplomas Sketch of planned research (2 pages each) indicating reference to the subject areas mentioned above Contact information of at least two referees Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 24 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Planned start date: 01/07/2026 Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL07935 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 85176 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) at the University of Luxembourg brings together expertise from the humanities, linguistics, cognitive sciences, social and educational sciences.People from across 20 disciplines are working within the Faculty. Along with the disciplinary approach a very ambitious interdisciplinary research culture has been developed. The faculty’s research and teaching focuses on social, economic, political and educational issues with the common goal of contributing to an inclusive, open and resourceful society. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-real-time-computational-biomechanics/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Real-Time Computational Biomechanics",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL07985 Your role You will join the Legato group, recognised internationally as a leading team in computational mechanics and surgical simulation, and work in tight collaboration with ARSPECTRA, world leader in medical AR glasses and navigation platforms. The focus of this position is the development of real-time, trustworthy biomechanical simulations for brain and skull, suitable for deployment on ARSPECTRA devices. You will work at the interface between finite-element modelling, software engineering and embedded/edge computing. Key Responasbilities: Develop and optimise finite-element models, e.g. Poisson, linear elasticity, large-deformation soft tissue, for real-time execution on AR devices and GPUs Implement these models within open-source frameworks such as SOFA, FEniCSx and SOniCS; experience with SOFA is a strong plus Design adaptive, error-controlled strategies that balance accuracy and speed under strict real-time constraints Benchmark and profile performance on ARSPECTRA hardware in collaboration with their engineering team Contribute to open-source code, demonstrators and joint publications with ARSPECTRA and clinical partners Your profile PhD in computational mechanics, applied mathematics, biomedical engineering, computer science or a closely related discipline Strong background in finite-element methods, continuum mechanics and numerical analysis Excellent programming skills in C++ and/or Python; experience with high-performance or real-time computing, e.g. GPU, multi-core, embedded, is desirable Prior experience with SOFA is a clear advantage; experience with FEniCSx, deal.II or similar frameworks is also relevant Interest in medical applications, AR/VR and interdisciplinary work with clinicians and industry We offer Multilingual and international character. Modern institution with a personal atmosphere. Staff coming from 90 countries. Member of the “University of the Greater Region” (UniGR) A modern and dynamic university. High-quality equipment. Close ties to the business world and to the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban site with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and with numerous non-academic partners such as ministries, local governments, associations, NGOs … How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL07985 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 85176 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-in-requirement-engineering-with-emphasis-on-regulatory-compliance-for-fintech/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Requirement Engineering with Emphasis on Regulatory Compliance for Fintech",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Kirchberg Campus Organisation Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) Job reference UOL08432 Your role We offer an attractive post-doctoral position in the context of the FutureFinTech, funded by the Luxembourg National Research Fund (FNR), aims to establish a Centre of Excellence in Financial Technologies. It develops AI- and software engineering-based solutions to automate the monitoring and verification of financial services’ compliance with regulatory requirements. Within its lighthouse on AI, compliance, and risk management, FutureFinTech leverages advanced AI techniques to analyze and operationalize regulations, enabling automated compliance assessment and risk management. The position holder will be required to perform the following tasks: Carrying out research in the predefined areas Implementing prototype tools Managing and contributing to national and international research projects Preparing project deliverables Disseminating results through scientific publications Presenting results in well-known international conferences and workshops Providing guidance to PhD, MSc, and BSc students Organizing relevant workshops and demonstrations Participating in proposal drafting to attract industrial, national, and European projects Your profile We are looking for a motivated candidate who can work independently and efficiently, is proactive in solving problems, and has strong analytical skills. The candidate should be interested in working in an international team with a multi-disciplinary set of backgrounds, where sharing resources and teamwork is essential. Qualification: PhD degree in Computer Science, Informatics, or Software Engineering Experience: Expertise, supported by a sound publication track record in relevant international conferences and top journals, in the following topics: Requirements Engineering Natural Language Processing and Understanding Text mining and information extraction Proficiency in Python Experience with information extraction from legal documents would be considered an advantage Language Skills: Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English (C1) are required We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter detailing your motivation for applying to the advertised research topic and/or project, including how your background, interests, and career goals align with its objective PhD diploma or a letter/information indicating the expected defense date Transcript of all modules and results from university-level courses taken List of publications Names, contact information and current position of 1-2 referees who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate their relationship to you Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 12 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Kirchberg Campus Internal Title: Postdoctoral researcher Job Reference: UOL08432 The yearly gross salary for every Postdoctoral Researcher at the UL is EUR 87306 (full time). About us The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Interdisciplinary Centre for Security, Reliability and Trust (SnT) at the University of Luxembourg is a leading international research and innovation centre in secure, reliable and trustworthy ICT systems and services.We play an instrumental role in Europe by fueling innovation through research partnerships with industry, boosting R&D investments leading to economic growth, and attracting highly qualified talent. We look for researchers from diverse academic backgrounds to contribute to our projects in areas such as: Network Security, Information Assurance, Model-driven Security, Cloud Computing, Cryptography, Satellite Systems, Vehicular Networks, and ICT Services & Applications. The successful candidate will join the SVV research group, headed by Prof. Domenico Bianculli. The group focuses on the development and design of reliable, safe, and secure software systems, carrying out both upstream activities such as requirements quality assurance and regulatory compliance, as well as downstream verification & validation activities, such as software testing and runtime verification. For further information, you may refer to https://www.uni.lu/snt-en/research-groups/svv. The successful candidate will work with Dr. Sallam Abualhaija and Prof. Domenico Bianculli Apply online Location Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-and-development-specialist-in-clinical-data-science-and-machine-learning/": {
      "title": "Research and Development Specialist in Clinical Data Science and Machine Learning",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Fixed-term contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Luxembourg Centre for Systems Biomedicine (LCSB) Job reference UOL08208 Your role Develop and optimize data processing pipelines for structured, semi‑structured, and unstructured clinical data Build, test, and deploy end‑to‑end AI workflows, including data ingestion, preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and inference Design and develop Retrieval‑Augmented Generation pipelines using embeddings, vector stores, and clinical knowledge sources Perform fine‑tuning of foundation models, including transformers and domain‑specific clinical models. Develop GenAI application workflows using APIs, e.g., Mistral, Anthropic, OpenAI, local open‑source models, agent frameworks Implement multilingual NLP pipelines – NER, entity linking, summarization, and ontology alignment Contribute to OMOP/FHIR‑based data harmonization workflows Support the development of agentic AI systems for clinical reasoning and decision support Contribute to documentation, scientific publications, and stakeholder engagement For further information, please contact Dr. Sandrine Medves (email address: sandrine.medves@uni.lu ). Your profile Master’s in Computer Science, AI/ML, Biomedical Engineering, Bioinformatics, Health Informatics, or related fields Demonstrated hands‑on experience in designing, implementing, and deploying AI workflows—including preprocessing pipelines, model training, optimization, and deployment into production or research environments Proven expertise with: RAG pipeline development: vector databases, embedding models, retrieval optimization GenAI workflows using APIs: prompt chaining, orchestrators, model evaluation Fine‑tuning LLMs or domain‑specific models: supervised fine‑tuning, PEFT, LoRA, adapters Solid experience in Machine learning / deep learning frameworks, e.g., PyTorch or TensorFlow, and Data engineering, e.g. Python, Spark, SQL, NLP and transformer‑based architectures Experience with health data standards such as HL7 FHIR, OMOP CDM is a strong asset Experience working with clinical datasets, EHR systems, or biomedical text is highly desirable Knowledge of privacy‑preserving computation, such as federated learning, differential privacy, is a plus Interest in dementia, ageing, or neurological disorders is advantageous Fluency in English is required We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Names, contact information and current position of 1-2 referees who can, upon request, provide an assessment of the application. Please indicate their relationship to you Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract 36 Month Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Research and development specialist Job Reference: UOL08208 . About the LCSB The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Luxembourg Centre for Systems Biomedicine (LCSB) is an interdisciplinary research centre of the University of Luxembourg. We conduct fundamental and translational research in the field of Systems Biology and Biomedicine – in the lab, in the clinic and in silico. We focus on neurodegenerative processes and are especially interested in Alzheimer’s and Parkinson’s disease and their contributing factors. The LCSB recruits talented scientists from various disciplines: computer scientists, mathematicians, biologists, chemists, engineers, physicists and clinicians from more than 50 countries currently work at the LCSB. We excel because we are truly interdisciplinary, and together we contribute to science and society. Successful candidate will join the Clinical and Translational Informatics, led by Dr. Venkata Satagopam, which focuses on bridging translational medicine and bioinformatics through innovative data integration, visualisation, and advanced analytics. Our research integrates bioinformatics, data science, and IT solutions to advance digital health and translational medicine using a “bench-to-bedside” approach. By harmonising and analysing diverse biomedical data, while focusing on the secure data processing and predictive modelling, we aim to drive progress in translational medicine, improving diagnostics and healthcare solutions. For more information, please visit our page . Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/research-support-technician/": {
      "title": "Research Support Technician",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Permanent contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) Job reference UOL08423 Your role Support practical teaching activities in Chemistry (main focus) and Biochemistry, mainly for the teaching programmes in Medicine and Life sciences Prepare daily the practical teaching sessions Ensure the maintenance and servicing of teaching laboratories and equipment Ensure consumable management and reconditioning of the teaching room and equipment after use Perform ordering, inventory updating, cleaning and storage of the equipment Contribute to the updating of the teaching support documentation Contribute to the general safety and development of the laboratories Support public engagement activities requiring practical sessions Cooperate closely with and support the teaching staff Your profile Minimal degree: Bachelor in chemistry/ biochemistry or related field Previous professional experience as chemistry/biochemistry laboratory technician Rigor, autonomy and organizational skills Ideally strong expertise in inorganic and organic chemistry and corresponding laboratory techniques Knowledge of biochemistry or molecular biology and corresponding techniques is an asset Knowledge of laboratory safety procedures Excellent practice of MS Office software and PC management Excellent communication and relationship skills Excellent practice of English (C1). Knowledge of French and/or German (B1) is an asset We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter (max. 1 page, EN, stating your motivation and mentioning a list of at least 5 experimental skills) Copy of diploma(s), including grade reports. Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Permanent Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Planned start date: February 2027 Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Research support technician Job Reference: UOL08423 . About the FSTM The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Science, Technology and Medicine (FSTM) at the University of Luxembourg contributes multidisciplinary expertise in the fields of Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Life Sciences and Medicine. Through its dual mission of teaching and research, the FSTM seeks to generate and disseminate knowledge and train new generations of responsible citizens in order to better understand, explain and advance society and the environment we live in. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
    },
    "https://www.uni.lu/en/jobs/study-programme-administrator/": {
      "title": "Study Programme Administrator",
      "description": "Job details Contract type Permanent contract – Full time Location Belval Campus Organisation Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) Job reference UOL08469 Your role Perform planning, scheduling and system update functions required for courses, exams and events Organise the courses and the exams per semester Inform and advise students and teachers on administrative and organisational matters General office duties: archiving, records management, welcoming students and teaching staff Maintain processes and procedures in line with the Faculty and University guidelines Participation in different events: meetings, visits, open days, student fairs, graduation ceremonies Your profile High school diploma in business administration or a Higher education degree Work experience in administration or in the education sector Work experience in Education or Training programmes is an asset Agile with IT tools and database. Digitally curious and eager to learn new technologies Team player, diplomatic, friendly, service-oriented Excellent organisational skills with attention to detail and accuracy Reliable and proactive Excellent command (C1) in French, English and German is required. Luxembourgish is an asset; We offer A modern, dynamic university with a personal and inclusive atmosphere. Multilingual and international character. Staff coming from more than 90 countries. Member of The Guild of European Research Intensive Universities An exceptional research environment, supported by skilled staff and high-quality equipment. Strong links to professional sectors and the Luxembourg labour market. A unique urban campus with excellent infrastructure A partner for society and industry. Cooperation with European institutions, innovative companies, the Financial Centre and a wide range of non-academic partners including ministries, local governments, associations, and NGOs How to apply Applications should include: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Early application is highly encouraged, as the applications will be processed upon reception. Please apply ONLINE formally through the HR system. Applications by Email will not be considered. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. In line with our values, the University of Luxembourg promotes an inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and are dedicated to upholding equality and respect for our employees and students. General information: Contract Type: Permanent Work Hours: Full Time 40.0 Hours per Week Location: Belval Campus Internal Title: Study programme administrator Job Reference: UOL08469 . About the FHSE The University of Luxembourg is an international research university with a distinctly multilingual and interdisciplinary character. The Faculty of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (FHSE) at the University of Luxembourg brings together expertise from the humanities, linguistics, cognitive sciences, social and educational sciences. People from across 20 disciplines are working within the Faculty. Along with the disciplinary approach a very ambitious interdisciplinary research culture has been developed. The faculty’s research and teaching focuses on social, economic, political and educational issues with the common goal of contributing to an inclusive, open and resourceful society. Apply online Location + − Leaflet Learn more University ‘s profile How the University is organised UMatter support network Share this share share email"
